# Properties

property.tooltip = {help, select, none {} other {{help}\n\n}}Available as `{id}` in editor scripts.

# Properties: universal

property.blend-mode = Blend Mode
property.blend-mode.tooltip = Controls how this item's pixels combine with graphics behind it. **Alpha** gives normal transparency, **Add** brightens, **Multiply** darkens, and **Screen** produces a softer brightening effect; available modes depend on the item type.
property.id = Id
property.id.tooltip = The identifier used to address this collection instance, game object, or component at runtime. It must be unique among its siblings; together with the hierarchy, it forms the item's URL.
property.image = Image
property.image.tooltip = The source image file used to build this resource. In an atlas it is one image to be packed; in a tile source it contains the grid of tiles.
property.material = Material
property.material.tooltip = The material used to render this item. It defines the shaders and their inputs, so choose one compatible with the item's geometry and textures.
property.name = Name
property.name.tooltip = The name used to identify this entry or resource. Use a unique, descriptive name when other entries or runtime APIs need to refer to it.
property.path = Path
property.path.tooltip = The project resource used as the prototype for this referenced collection, game object, or component. Changes to the prototype are reflected in every instance, while instance-specific property overrides remain local.
property.position = Position
property.position.tooltip = The item's translation along the X, Y, and Z axes, relative to its parent. Moving a parent also moves its children.
property.rotation = Rotation
property.rotation.tooltip = The item's orientation around the X, Y, and Z axes in degrees, relative to its parent. Rotating a parent also rotates its children.
property.scale = Scale
property.scale.tooltip = Multiplies the item's size along the X, Y, and Z axes relative to its parent. A value of `1` keeps the original scale.
property.size = Size
property.size.tooltip = The item's width, height, and, where applicable, depth. When read-only, the size is calculated automatically from the item's content or rendering resources. For GUI nodes, size also defines the bounds used for input picking.
property.url = URL
property.url.tooltip = The read-only runtime address derived from the hierarchy and **Id**. It targets a game object or component, or serves as the address prefix for the contents of a collection instance.

# Properties: appmanifest

property.appmanifest.physics-2d = Physics 2D
property.appmanifest.physics-2d.tooltip = Select the Box2D implementation to include, or **None** to remove 2D physics and reduce the engine size. Box2D 3 may behave differently from the legacy implementation, so existing projects may need physics adjustments.
property.appmanifest.physics-3d = Physics 3D
property.appmanifest.physics-3d.tooltip = Include the Bullet 3D physics engine. Disable this when the project does not use 3D physics to reduce the engine size.
property.appmanifest.rig+model = Rig + Model
property.appmanifest.rig+model.tooltip = Choose whether to include both model rendering and rig animation, rig functionality only, or neither. Excluding unused functionality reduces the engine size.
property.appmanifest.exclude-record = Exclude Record
property.appmanifest.exclude-record.tooltip = Remove desktop video-recording support used by the `start_record` system message. Enable this when the project does not record gameplay to reduce the engine size.
property.appmanifest.profiler = Profiler
property.appmanifest.profiler.tooltip = Choose which builds include profiler functionality. **Debug Only** excludes it from release builds, **None** excludes it entirely, and **Always** also includes it in release builds.
property.appmanifest.exclude-sound = Exclude Sound
property.appmanifest.exclude-sound.tooltip = Remove all sound playback functionality from the engine. Enable this only when the project does not play audio.
property.appmanifest.exclude-gui = Exclude GUI
property.appmanifest.exclude-gui.tooltip = Remove GUI resources, components, and Lua support from the engine. Enable this only when the project does not use GUI scenes or scripts.
property.appmanifest.exclude-particle-fx = Exclude Particle FX
property.appmanifest.exclude-particle-fx.tooltip = Remove particle effect resources, components, and Lua support, including particle nodes in GUI scenes. GUI scenes without particle nodes remain supported.
property.appmanifest.exclude-tilemap = Exclude Tilemaps
property.appmanifest.exclude-tilemap.tooltip = Remove tilemap resources, components, and Lua support from the engine. Enable this only when the project does not use tilemaps.
property.appmanifest.exclude-sound-decoder-wav = Exclude Sound Decoder: WAV
property.appmanifest.exclude-sound-decoder-wav.tooltip = Remove support for `.wav` sound resources. Enable this only when the project does not play WAV audio.
property.appmanifest.exclude-sound-decoder-ogg = Exclude Sound Decoder: OGG
property.appmanifest.exclude-sound-decoder-ogg.tooltip = Remove support for Ogg Vorbis sound resources. Enable this only when the project does not play `.ogg` audio.
property.appmanifest.include-sound-decoder-opus = Include Sound Decoder: Opus
property.appmanifest.include-sound-decoder-opus.tooltip = Include support for Ogg Opus sound resources. The Opus decoder is excluded by default and is required to play `.opus` audio.
property.appmanifest.exclude-input = Exclude Input
property.appmanifest.exclude-input.tooltip = Remove all input handling from the engine. Enable this only when the project does not use keyboard, mouse, touch, gamepad, or other input.
property.appmanifest.exclude-liveupdate = Exclude Live Update
property.appmanifest.exclude-liveupdate.tooltip = Remove Live Update functionality used to mount resources excluded from the initial bundle. Enable this only when the project does not download and mount Live Update content.
property.appmanifest.exclude-image = Exclude Image
property.appmanifest.exclude-image.tooltip = Remove the `image` Lua module from the engine. Enable this only when project scripts do not use its image-loading and image-data functions.
property.appmanifest.exclude-types = Exclude Types
property.appmanifest.exclude-types.tooltip = Remove the `types` Lua module from the engine. Enable this only when project scripts do not use its type-checking functions.
property.appmanifest.exclude-basis-transcoder = Exclude Basis Transcoder
property.appmanifest.exclude-basis-transcoder.tooltip = Remove the Basis Universal texture transcoder. Enable this only when no texture profile uses Basis Universal compression.
property.appmanifest.use-android-support-lib = Use Android Support Library
property.appmanifest.use-android-support-lib.tooltip = Use the deprecated Android Support Library instead of AndroidX. Enable this only for legacy dependencies that have not migrated to AndroidX.
property.appmanifest.graphics = Graphics
property.appmanifest.graphics.tooltip = Select the graphics backend included in Windows and Linux builds. Including both OpenGL and Vulkan permits a fallback when the preferred backend is unavailable, but increases engine size.
property.appmanifest.graphics-osx = Graphics (macOS)
property.appmanifest.graphics-osx.tooltip = Select the graphics backend included in macOS builds. Vulkan is the default; a combined choice includes a fallback backend but increases engine size.
property.appmanifest.graphics-ios = Graphics (iOS)
property.appmanifest.graphics-ios.tooltip = Select the graphics backend included in iOS builds. OpenGL is the default; a combined choice includes a fallback backend but increases engine size.
property.appmanifest.graphics-android = Graphics (Android)
property.appmanifest.graphics-android.tooltip = Select the graphics backend included in Android builds. The default includes both, preferring Vulkan when available and falling back to OpenGL ES.
property.appmanifest.graphics-web = Graphics (HTML5)
property.appmanifest.graphics-web.tooltip = Select the graphics backend included in HTML5 builds. WebGL is the default; including both WebGL and WebGPU permits fallback but increases engine size.
property.appmanifest.use-font-layout = Use full text layout system
property.appmanifest.use-font-layout.tooltip = Include the full text layout system required for runtime SDF font generation from TrueType fonts. Runtime glyph rasterization also requires `font.runtime_generation` in `game.project`; it supports features such as right-to-left text.
property.appmanifest.exclude-rich-text = Exclude Rich Text
property.appmanifest.exclude-rich-text.tooltip = Replace rich text parsing and style effects with a null implementation to reduce engine size. Plain text layout and rendering remain available.

# Properties: atlas

property.atlas.animation.id.tooltip = The identifier used to select this flip-book animation in components and runtime animation APIs. It must be unique within the atlas.
property.atlas.animation.fps = FPS
property.atlas.animation.fps.tooltip = The animation playback speed in frames per second. Higher values display the frames more quickly.
property.atlas.animation.flip-horizontal = Flip Horizontal
property.atlas.animation.flip-horizontal.tooltip = Mirror every animation frame horizontally during playback.
property.atlas.animation.flip-vertical = Flip Vertical
property.atlas.animation.flip-vertical.tooltip = Mirror every animation frame vertically during playback.
property.atlas.animation.playback = Playback
property.atlas.animation.playback.tooltip = Choose whether the animation remains on its first frame, plays once, or loops, and whether frames run forward, backward, or ping-pong. **Once Ping Pong** stops after returning to the second frame to avoid repeating the first frame when animations are chained.
property.atlas.image.id.tooltip = The read-only identifier derived from the source image's base name after applying **Rename Patterns**. It is used to select the image and to match corresponding frames across atlases.
property.atlas.image.pivot = Pivot
property.atlas.image.pivot.tooltip = The point aligned with the component's position when this image is displayed. `(0, 0)` is top-left, `(1, 1)` bottom-right, and `(0.5, 0.5)` center; values outside this range are allowed.
property.atlas.image.sprite-trim-mode = Sprite Trim Mode
property.atlas.image.sprite-trim-mode.tooltip = Approximate the image's non-transparent area with the selected number of vertices instead of rendering its full rectangle. This can reduce transparent overdraw, but cannot be used with slice-9 sprites.
property.atlas.margin = Margin
property.atlas.margin.tooltip = The number of pixels inserted between packed images in the atlas texture.
property.atlas.inner-padding = Inner Padding
property.atlas.inner-padding.tooltip = The number of empty pixels added around each image before it is packed into the atlas.
property.atlas.extrude-borders = Extrude Borders
property.atlas.extrude-borders.tooltip = The number of times each image's edge pixels are copied outward. This prevents neighboring images from bleeding into the image when a shader samples near its edge.
property.atlas.max-page-width = Max Page Width
property.atlas.max-page-height = Max Page Height
property.atlas.max-page-size = Max Page Size
property.atlas.max-page-size.tooltip = The maximum width and height of each page in a multi-page atlas. Set both values above zero to enable paging; components that use the atlas must use a paged-atlas material.
property.atlas.rename-patterns = Rename Patterns
property.atlas.rename-patterns.tooltip = Comma-separated `search=replace` patterns applied to every image's base name. For example, `hat=cat,_normal=` changes `hat_normal` to `cat`; matching names are useful when corresponding frames come from multiple atlases.

# Properties: camera

property.camera.aspect-ratio = Aspect Ratio
property.camera.aspect-ratio.tooltip = **Perspective only.** Ratio of the view frustum's width to its height. Use `1.0` for square, about `1.33` for 4:3, or about `1.78` for 16:9; ignored when **Auto Aspect Ratio** is enabled.
property.camera.fov = FOV
property.camera.fov.tooltip = **Perspective only.** Vertical field of view in radians. Higher values show more of the scene; for example, 60° is about `1.047` radians.
property.camera.near-z = Near Z
property.camera.near-z.tooltip = Signed view-space depth of the near clipping plane. Geometry outside the interval between **Near Z** and **Far Z** is clipped.
property.camera.far-z = Far Z
property.camera.far-z.tooltip = Signed view-space depth of the far clipping plane. A smaller interval between **Near Z** and **Far Z** improves depth-buffer precision but may clip geometry.
property.camera.auto-aspect-ratio = Auto Aspect Ratio
property.camera.auto-aspect-ratio.tooltip = **Perspective only.** Calculates the aspect ratio from the current window width and height instead of using **Aspect Ratio**.
property.camera.orthographic-projection = Orthographic Projection
property.camera.orthographic-projection.tooltip = Uses an orthographic projection, where objects remain the same apparent size regardless of their distance from the camera. Commonly used for 2D scenes.
property.camera.orthographic-zoom = Orthographic Zoom
property.camera.orthographic-zoom.tooltip = **Orthographic only.** Positive zoom multiplier: values above `1` zoom in and values below `1` zoom out. In **Auto Fit** and **Auto Cover**, it multiplies the automatically calculated zoom.
property.camera.orthographic-mode = Orthographic Zoom Mode
property.camera.orthographic-mode.tooltip = **Orthographic only.** **Fixed** uses **Orthographic Zoom** directly. **Auto Fit** keeps the full design area visible and may show extra content; **Auto Cover** fills the window and may crop content. Auto modes use the display width and height from `game.project` as the design size.

# Properties: collection proxy

property.collection-proxy.collection = Collection
property.collection-proxy.collection.tooltip = Collection loaded as a separate game world. After loading, `enable` initializes it first when needed. When unloading, `unload` finalizes it first when needed; explicit lifecycle messages remain available for manual control.
property.collection-proxy.exclude = Exclude
property.collection-proxy.exclude.tooltip = Excludes this proxy's content from the main bundle when publishing Live Update content, including resources not unique to one excluded proxy. Mount the required content before loading. **Build and Run** does not exclude it.

# Properties: collision object

property.collision-object.collision-shape = Collision Shape
property.collision-object.collision-shape.tooltip = An external tile map or convex shape that defines the object. Leave this unset when using primitive shapes added beneath the collision object.
property.collision-object.type = Type
property.collision-object.type.tooltip = **Dynamic** objects are simulated, **Kinematic** objects are moved and resolved by your code, **Static** objects do not move, and **Trigger** objects only detect overlaps. Available as `collision_type` in editor scripts; prefer it over `type`, which can be shadowed by an embedded component's type.
property.collision-object.mass = Mass
property.collision-object.mass.tooltip = Mass in kilograms used to simulate a **Dynamic** object. It must be greater than zero and is ignored for other object types.
property.collision-object.friction = Friction
property.collision-object.friction.tooltip = Resistance to sliding while objects are in contact. `0` gives no friction; values up to `1` are typical, and zero friction on either object makes the contact frictionless.
property.collision-object.restitution = Restitution
property.collision-object.restitution.tooltip = How much the object bounces after a collision. `0` gives no bounce and `1` is fully elastic; the final response also depends on the other object's restitution and the selected physics engine.
property.collision-object.linear-damping = Linear Damping
property.collision-object.linear-damping.tooltip = Gradually reduces linear velocity even when the object is not in contact with anything. Use values from `0` to `1` to simulate resistance such as drag.
property.collision-object.angular-damping = Angular Damping
property.collision-object.angular-damping.tooltip = Gradually reduces angular velocity, slowing the object's rotation even when it is not in contact with anything.
property.collision-object.locked-rotation = Locked Rotation
property.collision-object.locked-rotation.tooltip = Prevents the physics simulation from rotating the collision object in response to forces or collisions.
property.collision-object.bullet = Bullet
property.collision-object.bullet.tooltip = **2D physics only.** Enables continuous collision detection to keep fast-moving objects from passing through other dynamic objects. Only applies when **Type** is **Dynamic**.
property.collision-object.event-collision = Generate Collision Events
property.collision-object.event-collision.tooltip = Generates general collision notifications without contact-point details. Disabling it suppresses this object's `collision_response` messages; a centralized listener filters the interaction only when both objects disable it.
property.collision-object.event-contact = Generate Contact Events
property.collision-object.event-contact.tooltip = Generates detailed contact-point notifications, including position, normal, penetration, and impulse; several can occur for one object pair each frame. Disabling it suppresses this object's `contact_point_response` messages; a centralized listener filters the interaction only when both objects disable it.
property.collision-object.event-trigger = Generate Trigger Events
property.collision-object.event-trigger.tooltip = Generates notifications when an object enters or leaves a **Trigger**. Disabling it suppresses this object's `trigger_response` messages; a centralized listener filters the interaction only when both objects disable it.
property.collision-object.group = Group
property.collision-object.group.tooltip = The collision group this object belongs to. Two objects interact only when each object's **Mask** includes the other object's group.
property.collision-object.group.tilemap.tooltip = Not used when **Collision Shape** is a tile map; collision groups are defined by the tile map's tile source.
property.collision-object.mask = Mask
property.collision-object.mask.tooltip = Comma-separated collision groups this object can interact with. Both objects must include the other's group in their masks; an empty mask collides with nothing.
property.collision-object.shape.id.tooltip = The identifier of this embedded shape within its collision object. Use it with APIs such as `physics.get_shape()` and `physics.set_shape()` to inspect or resize the shape at runtime.
property.collision-object.shape.diameter = Diameter
property.collision-object.shape.diameter.tooltip = The full diameter of a sphere or the rounded cross-section of a capsule. Must be greater than zero.
property.collision-object.shape.dimensions = Dimensions
property.collision-object.shape.dimensions.tooltip = The box shape's full **Width**, **Height**, and **Depth**. **Depth** affects only 3D physics, but every dimension must be greater than zero.
property.collision-object.shape.height = Height
property.collision-object.shape.height.tooltip = **3D physics only.** The length of a capsule's straight section between its rounded ends. Its total end-to-end length is **Height + Diameter**.

