property.compute.compute-program = Compute Program

# Properties: cubemap

property.cubemap.back = Back
property.cubemap.back.tooltip = The image mapped to the cubemap's back-facing (`-Z`) side. Cubemaps are sampled by direction for effects such as skyboxes, reflections, and lighting; all six face images must have identical dimensions.
property.cubemap.bottom = Bottom
property.cubemap.bottom.tooltip = The image mapped to the cubemap's bottom-facing (`-Y`) side. Cubemaps are sampled by direction for effects such as skyboxes, reflections, and lighting; all six face images must have identical dimensions.
property.cubemap.front = Front
property.cubemap.front.tooltip = The image mapped to the cubemap's front-facing (`+Z`) side. Cubemaps are sampled by direction for effects such as skyboxes, reflections, and lighting; all six face images must have identical dimensions.
property.cubemap.left = Left
property.cubemap.left.tooltip = The image mapped to the cubemap's left-facing (`-X`) side. Cubemaps are sampled by direction for effects such as skyboxes, reflections, and lighting; all six face images must have identical dimensions.
property.cubemap.right = Right
property.cubemap.right.tooltip = The image mapped to the cubemap's right-facing (`+X`) side. Cubemaps are sampled by direction for effects such as skyboxes, reflections, and lighting; all six face images must have identical dimensions.
property.cubemap.top = Top
property.cubemap.top.tooltip = The image mapped to the cubemap's top-facing (`+Y`) side. Cubemaps are sampled by direction for effects such as skyboxes, reflections, and lighting; all six face images must have identical dimensions.

# Properties: factory

property.factory.prototype = Prototype
property.factory.prototype.tooltip = Resource instantiated by this component: a game object for a Factory or a collection for a Collection Factory. Spawn it with `factory.create()` or `collectionfactory.create()`.
property.factory.load-dynamically = Load Dynamically
property.factory.load-dynamically.tooltip = Postpones loading the prototype's resources until they are needed, but still includes them in the bundle. Calling `factory.create()` or `collectionfactory.create()` loads them synchronously and may cause a hitch; call `factory.load()` or `collectionfactory.load()` first to load them asynchronously.
property.factory.dynamic-prototype = Dynamic Prototype
property.factory.dynamic-prototype.tooltip = Allows `factory.set_prototype()` or `collectionfactory.set_prototype()` to replace the prototype at runtime. If the previous prototype was loaded with `factory.load()` or `collectionfactory.load()`, unload it before switching. This disables component-count optimization for the owning collection, so it uses the configured project maximums.

# Properties: font

property.font.font = Font
property.font.font.tooltip = Selects the source font: a TrueType (`.ttf`), OpenType (`.otf`), or BMFont (`.fnt`) file.
property.font.texture = Texture
property.font.texture.tooltip = The PNG glyph sheet referenced by this BMFont (`.fnt`) file. The texture must be in the same folder and match the filename declared by the BMFont.
property.font.output-format = Output Format
property.font.output-format.tooltip = **Bitmap** rasterizes TTF/OTF glyphs and is required for BMFont (`.fnt`) sources. **Distance Field** stores distance-to-edge data for cleaner scaling and requires a compatible distance-field material.
property.font.render-mode = Render Mode
property.font.render-mode.tooltip = **Single Layer** renders one quad per character. **Multi Layer** renders shadow, outline, and face separately, preventing wide outlines from covering neighboring glyphs and enabling **Shadow X/Y** offsets.
property.font.size = Size
property.font.size.tooltip = Target glyph size in pixels when generating the font. Bitmap fonts look best near this size; distance-field fonts need enough size to preserve shape detail when scaled up.
property.font.antialias = Antialias
property.font.antialias.tooltip = Smooths glyph edges when the font is rasterized. Disable it for pixel-perfect font rendering.
property.font.alpha = Alpha
property.font.alpha.tooltip = Controls the generated glyph face opacity from `0` (transparent) to `1` (opaque).
property.font.outline-alpha = Outline Alpha
property.font.outline-alpha.tooltip = Controls the generated outline opacity from `0` (transparent) to `1` (opaque). Use `0` to disable the outline.
property.font.outline-width = Outline Width
property.font.outline-width.tooltip = Width of the generated glyph outline in pixels. Use `0` for no outline.
property.font.shadow-alpha = Shadow Alpha
property.font.shadow-alpha.tooltip = Controls the generated shadow opacity from `0` (transparent) to `1` (opaque). Use `0` to disable the shadow.
property.font.shadow-blur = Shadow Blur
property.font.shadow-blur.tooltip = Softens the generated shadow. For bitmap output, this is the number of blur passes; for distance-field output, it is the blur width in pixels.
property.font.shadow-x = Shadow X
property.font.shadow-x.tooltip = Horizontal offset of the generated shadow in pixels. It affects glyph rendering only in **Multi Layer** mode.
property.font.shadow-y = Shadow Y
property.font.shadow-y.tooltip = Vertical offset of the generated shadow in pixels. It affects glyph rendering only in **Multi Layer** mode.
property.font.cache-width = Cache Width
property.font.cache-width.tooltip = Width in pixels of the glyph-cache texture used for rendering. Increase it if the cache runs out of cells; `0` uses automatic sizing.
property.font.cache-height = Cache Height
property.font.cache-height.tooltip = Height in pixels of the glyph-cache texture used for rendering. Increase it if the cache runs out of cells; `0` uses automatic sizing.
property.font.characters = Characters
property.font.characters.tooltip = Characters included when building an offline font; limiting this set reduces font size. For runtime fonts, these characters are generated up front to prewarm the glyph cache. Clearing the field restores printable ASCII.
property.font.all-chars = All Chars
property.font.all-chars.tooltip = For offline fonts, includes every glyph from the source instead of only **Characters**, which can greatly increase font size. For runtime fonts, glyphs are generated on demand and enabling this skips **Characters** prewarming.

# Properties: gui

property.gui.id.tooltip = The identifier used to find this node with `gui.get_node()`. It must be unique within the GUI scene; nodes from a template instance are prefixed with the template node's **Id** and a slash.
property.gui.adjust-mode = Adjust Mode
property.gui.adjust-mode.tooltip = Controls how the node's content adapts when its bounds are adjusted for a different screen size. **Fit** preserves aspect ratio inside the bounds, **Zoom** preserves it while covering the bounds, and **Stretch** fills the bounds. Ignored when **Adjust Reference** is **Disabled**; ParticleFX nodes do not support **Stretch**.
property.gui.adjust-reference = Adjust Reference
property.gui.adjust-reference.tooltip = Chooses the size used when adjusting nodes. **Per Node** uses the parent's adjusted size, or the scene for root nodes. **Disabled** turns adjustment off. **Root (Deprecated)** uses the scene size for every node.
property.gui.alpha = Alpha
property.gui.alpha.tooltip = Controls the node's opacity from `0` (transparent) to `1` (opaque). If **Inherit Alpha** is enabled, this value is multiplied by the parent's alpha.
property.gui.clipping-inverted = Clipping Inverted
property.gui.clipping-inverted.tooltip = Inverts this node's stencil mask, so its children are rendered outside the node's shape instead of inside it.
property.gui.clipping-mode = Clipping Mode
property.gui.clipping-mode.tooltip = **None** renders normally. **Stencil** uses the node's geometry as a mask that clips its child nodes; the texture's transparency does not shape the mask.
property.gui.clipping-visible = Clipping Visible
property.gui.clipping-visible.tooltip = Renders the clipping node's own content as well as using its geometry to mask child nodes. Disable it when the node should act only as a mask.
property.gui.color = Color
property.gui.color.tooltip = Sets the node's color. On textured box and pie nodes, it is multiplied with the texture, so white leaves the texture unchanged.
property.gui.current-nodes = Current Nodes
property.gui.current-nodes.tooltip = The number of nodes currently defined by this GUI scene. Use it as a baseline when choosing **Max Nodes**, leaving room for nodes created or cloned at runtime.
property.gui.enabled = Enabled
property.gui.enabled.tooltip = Disabled nodes are not rendered or animated and cannot be selected by `gui.pick_node()`. Use **Visible** instead when an invisible node must remain active and pickable.
property.gui.font = Font
property.gui.font.tooltip = Selects the font used to render this text node. The font must first be added under the GUI scene's **Fonts** section.
property.gui.resource.font = Font
property.gui.resource.font.tooltip = Selects the font resource exposed by this entry in the GUI scene's **Fonts** section. Text nodes select the entry by its **Name**.
property.gui.inherit-alpha = Inherit Alpha
property.gui.inherit-alpha.tooltip = Multiplies this node's alpha by its parent's alpha. Enable it when fading a parent should also fade this node.
property.gui.inner-radius = Inner Radius
property.gui.inner-radius.tooltip = Sets the radius of the empty center of a pie node, measured along the X axis. Use `0` for a solid pie and increase it to create a ring.
property.gui.layer = Layer
property.gui.layer.tooltip = Assigns the node to a GUI layer, whose order overrides normal node and hierarchy draw order. An unset layer inherits from the parent, or uses the default layer drawn before named layers.
property.gui.line-break = Line Break
property.gui.line-break.tooltip = Wraps text across multiple lines at the node's width. Text can break only where it contains suitable whitespace.
property.gui.max-dynamic-textures = Max Dynamic Textures
property.gui.max-dynamic-textures.tooltip = Maximum number of runtime textures tracked by this GUI. This includes textures created with `gui.new_texture()` and external textures assigned to the component; raise it when replacing many such textures.
property.gui.max-nodes = Max Nodes
property.gui.max-nodes.tooltip = Maximum number of nodes this GUI can hold, including nodes created or cloned at runtime. Keep it above **Current Nodes** with enough headroom for the largest runtime node count.
property.gui.outline = Outline
property.gui.outline.tooltip = Sets the outline color of text rendered by this node. The font resource controls the outline's generated shape and width.
property.gui.outline-alpha = Outline Alpha
property.gui.outline-alpha.tooltip = Controls the text outline's opacity from `0` (transparent) to `1` (opaque).
property.gui.outer-bounds = Outer Bounds
property.gui.outer-bounds.tooltip = Chooses the outer shape of a pie node. **Ellipse** follows the outer radius; **Rectangle** extends the pie to the node's bounding box.
property.gui.perimeter-vertices = Perimeter Vertices
property.gui.perimeter-vertices.tooltip = Number of vertices used for the full 360-degree perimeter of a pie node. Higher values make curved edges smoother but add geometry; valid values are `4`–`1000`.
property.gui.particlefx = ParticleFX
property.gui.particlefx.tooltip = Selects the particle effect played by this GUI node in screen space. The effect must first be added under the GUI scene's **ParticleFX** section.
property.gui.resource.particlefx = ParticleFX
property.gui.resource.particlefx.tooltip = Selects the particle effect exposed by this entry in the GUI scene's **ParticleFX** section. ParticleFX nodes select the entry by its **Name**.
property.gui.pie-fill-angle = Pie Fill Angle
property.gui.pie-fill-angle.tooltip = Sets how much of a pie node is filled, in degrees counter-clockwise from the right side of the node.
property.gui.pivot = Pivot
property.gui.pivot.tooltip = Sets the node's reference point for position, rotation, scaling, and resizing. On text nodes, west pivots left-align text, east pivots right-align it, and the remaining pivots center-align it.
property.gui.script = Script
property.gui.script.tooltip = Assigns the GUI script that controls this scene's logic, input, messages, and node manipulation at runtime. A GUI scene can have one script.
property.gui.shadow = Shadow
property.gui.shadow.tooltip = Sets the shadow color of text rendered by this node. The font resource and font material determine how the shadow is generated and rendered.
property.gui.shadow-alpha = Shadow Alpha
property.gui.shadow-alpha.tooltip = Controls the text shadow's opacity from `0` (transparent) to `1` (opaque).
property.gui.size-mode = Size Mode
property.gui.size-mode.tooltip = **Auto** uses the assigned image or animation frame's size. Without a texture, the editable **Size** is used. **Manual** always uses **Size** for rendering and input picking.
property.gui.slice9 = Slice 9
property.gui.slice9.tooltip = Preserves texture borders when a box node is resized. Set the unscaled margins in pixels as **Left**, **Top**, **Right**, and **Bottom**; corners stay fixed while edges and the center stretch.
property.gui.texture = Texture
property.gui.texture.tooltip = Selects the image or flip-book animation drawn on a box or pie node. The atlas or tile source must first be added under the GUI scene's **Textures** section.
property.gui.resource.texture = Texture
property.gui.resource.texture.tooltip = Selects the atlas or tile source exposed by this entry in the GUI scene's **Textures** section. Box and pie nodes select its images or animations by entry name.
property.gui.template = Template
property.gui.template.tooltip = Selects a GUI scene to instantiate as a reusable node hierarchy. Instance properties can override template values; the template entry itself does not exist as a runtime node.
property.gui.text = Text
property.gui.text.tooltip = The text displayed by this text node. Change it at runtime with `gui.set_text()`.
property.gui.text-leading = Text Leading
property.gui.text-leading.tooltip = Scales the spacing between lines of text. `1` is normal line spacing and `0` removes the spacing.
property.gui.text-tracking = Text Tracking
property.gui.text-tracking.tooltip = Scales the spacing between characters. The default `0` applies no additional letter spacing.
property.gui.visible = Visible
property.gui.visible.tooltip = Invisible nodes are not rendered, but remain animated and can still be selected by `gui.pick_node()`. Disable **Enabled** as well when the node should be inactive.
property.gui.x-anchor = X Anchor
property.gui.x-anchor.tooltip = Controls horizontal positioning when the parent or scene is resized. **Left** and **Right** keep the pivot at the same proportional distance from that edge; **None** keeps it relative to the adjusted center.
property.gui.y-anchor = Y Anchor
property.gui.y-anchor.tooltip = Controls vertical positioning when the parent or scene is resized. **Top** and **Bottom** keep the pivot at the same proportional distance from that edge; **None** keeps it relative to the adjusted center.

# Properties: label

property.label.color = Color
property.label.color.tooltip = Sets the text's RGBA color. Use the alpha channel to control opacity.
property.label.font = Font
property.label.font.tooltip = Selects the font resource used to render the label. The label's material must be compatible with the font type: bitmap, distance field, or BMFont.
property.label.leading = Leading
property.label.leading.tooltip = Scales the spacing between lines of text. `1` is normal line spacing and `0` removes the spacing.
property.label.line-break = Line Break
property.label.line-break.tooltip = Wraps text across multiple lines at the label's **Size** width. Text can break only where it contains suitable whitespace.
property.label.outline = Outline
property.label.outline.tooltip = Sets the text outline's RGBA color. The font resource controls the generated outline shape and width; set this color's alpha to `0` to hide it.
property.label.pivot = Pivot
property.label.pivot.tooltip = Sets the label's reference point and text alignment. West pivots left-align text, east pivots right-align it, and the remaining pivots center-align it.
property.label.shadow = Shadow
property.label.shadow.tooltip = Sets the text shadow's RGBA color. The font resource defines the shadow, while the material determines whether it is rendered; the default label material disables shadows.
property.label.size = Size
property.label.size.tooltip = Sets the label's text bounding box. When **Line Break** is enabled, the width determines where text wraps.
property.label.text = Text
property.label.text.tooltip = The text displayed by this label. Change it at runtime with `label.set_text()`.
property.label.tracking = Tracking
property.label.tracking.tooltip = Scales the spacing between characters. The default `0` applies no additional letter spacing.

# Properties: light

property.light.color = Color
property.light.color.tooltip = Sets the light's RGB color. The alpha channel is ignored.
property.light.intensity = Intensity
property.light.intensity.tooltip = Multiplies the light's color contribution. Use `0` for no contribution; the material shader determines how the resulting light data affects surfaces.
property.light.range = Range
property.light.range.tooltip = Radius of a point or spot light in world units. The effective range is multiplied by the smallest absolute axis of the game object's world scale.
property.light.inner-cone-angle = Inner Cone Angle
property.light.inner-cone-angle.tooltip = Angle in degrees within which a spot light has full strength. It must be between `0` and the **Outer Cone Angle**.
property.light.outer-cone-angle = Outer Cone Angle
property.light.outer-cone-angle.tooltip = Angle in degrees defining a spot light's outer edge. The light fades between the inner and outer cones; valid values are `0`–`180` and cannot be less than the **Inner Cone Angle**.

# Properties: mesh

property.mesh.normal-stream = Normal Stream
property.mesh.normal-stream.tooltip = Selects the buffer stream that contains vertex normals. An empty value uses the stream named `normal`; a stream must be selected explicitly when the material uses **World Space** so the engine can transform it correctly.
property.mesh.position-stream = Position Stream
property.mesh.position-stream.tooltip = Selects the buffer stream that contains vertex positions. An empty value uses the stream named `position`; a stream must be selected explicitly when the material uses **World Space** so the engine can transform it correctly.
property.mesh.primitive-type = Primitive Type
property.mesh.primitive-type.tooltip = Controls how sequential vertices form geometry: **Lines** uses independent pairs, **Triangles** uses independent groups of three, and **Triangle Strip** adds a triangle for each vertex after the first two.
property.mesh.vertices = Vertices
property.mesh.vertices.tooltip = Selects the `.buffer` resource containing the mesh's per-vertex streams, such as positions, normals, colors, and texture coordinates. Its contents can be replaced at runtime with `resource.set_buffer()`.

# Properties: model

property.model.animations = Animations
property.model.animations.tooltip = Animation Set, glTF, or GLB resource containing the skeletal or morph-target animations available to this model. Select one of its animation ids as **Default Animation** or play it with `model.play_anim()`.
property.model.create-go-bones = Create GO Bones
property.model.create-go-bones.tooltip = Creates a runtime game object for every skeleton bone, allowing attachments such as a weapon parented to a hand bone. Bone objects can be found with `model.get_go()` and count toward the collection's game-object capacity.
property.model.default-animation = Default Animation
property.model.default-animation.tooltip = Animation from **Animations** that starts automatically with the model. Leave empty when animation should be started explicitly with `model.play_anim()`.
property.model.mesh = Mesh
property.model.mesh.tooltip = glTF or GLB resource containing the model's visible geometry. Morph targets are imported together with the mesh.
property.model.skeleton = Skeleton
property.model.skeleton.tooltip = glTF or GLB resource containing the bone hierarchy used for skeletal animation. Defold imports the first skin in the file; this is often the same resource used for **Mesh**.

# Properties: particlefx

property.particlefx.category.particle-life = Particle Life

property.particlefx.id.tooltip = The emitter identifier. Use it to target a specific emitter when setting or resetting ParticleFX render constants and emitter properties at runtime.
property.particlefx.animation = Animation
property.particlefx.animation.tooltip = Selects the image or flip-book animation from **Image** to render on each particle.
property.particlefx.duration = Duration
property.particlefx.duration.tooltip = Number of seconds the emitter produces particles before stopping or looping. The **±** value randomly varies the actual duration within that range.
property.particlefx.inherit-velocity = Inherit Velocity
property.particlefx.inherit-velocity.tooltip = Portion of the emitter's estimated velocity added to newly spawned particles. Available in **World** emission space; `0` inherits none and `1` inherits all.
property.particlefx.material = Material
property.particlefx.material.tooltip = Selects the material used to shade and render particles from this emitter. Its shader, samplers, and vertex attributes must suit particle rendering.
property.particlefx.max-particle-count = Max Particle Count
property.particlefx.max-particle-count.tooltip = Maximum number of this emitter's particles that may exist simultaneously. New particles are skipped while the limit is full; higher limits reserve more memory.
property.particlefx.mode = Play Mode
property.particlefx.mode.tooltip = **Once** stops emitting after **Duration**. **Loop** restarts the emitter timeline whenever the duration is reached.
property.particlefx.particle-orientation = Particle Orientation
property.particlefx.particle-orientation.tooltip = Controls particle rotation: **Default** starts from the emitter orientation, **Initial Direction** aligns once to the launch direction, **Movement Direction** follows velocity, and **Angular Velocity** rotates using the angular-velocity properties.
property.particlefx.pivot = Pivot
property.particlefx.pivot.tooltip = Offsets each particle's image relative to its position before rotation and scaling. `(0, 0, 0)` centers the image; positive X or Y moves it right or up.
property.particlefx.size-mode = Size Mode
property.particlefx.size-mode.tooltip = For a playing flip-book animation, **Auto** uses each frame's source dimensions and ignores **Initial Size**. **Manual** uses **Initial Size** to control particle dimensions.
property.particlefx.space = Emission Space
property.particlefx.space.tooltip = **World** leaves spawned particles independent of later emitter movement. **Emitter** keeps them relative to the moving and rotating emitter.
property.particlefx.start-delay = Start Delay
property.particlefx.start-delay.tooltip = Number of seconds to wait before the emitter starts producing particles. The **±** value randomly varies the actual delay within that range.
property.particlefx.start-offset = Start Offset
property.particlefx.start-offset.tooltip = Prewarms the effect by simulating it before it first becomes visible. The effective offset is limited to the emitter's maximum particle lifetime.
property.particlefx.stretch-with-velocity = Stretch With Velocity
property.particlefx.stretch-with-velocity.tooltip = Multiplies **Stretch Y** by particle speed, making faster particles more stretched. Use **Movement Direction** orientation to align that stretch with velocity.
property.particlefx.tile-source = Image
property.particlefx.tile-source.tooltip = Selects the atlas or tile source that supplies particle images and flip-book animations.
property.particlefx.type = Emitter Type
property.particlefx.type.tooltip = Sets the emitter's spawn shape and launch directions. **Circle** and **Sphere** emit outward, **2D Cone** and **Cone** emit through their top, and **Box** emits along local Y.

property.particlefx.emitter-key-particle-alpha = Initial Alpha
property.particlefx.emitter-key-particle-alpha.tooltip = Alpha tint assigned when each particle spawns. It can vary randomly by **Spread** and follow a curve over the emitter's duration; the particle-life **Alpha** curve multiplies it later.
property.particlefx.emitter-key-particle-angular-velocity = Initial Angular Velocity
property.particlefx.emitter-key-particle-angular-velocity.tooltip = Initial rotation speed in degrees per second. It can vary by **Spread** and over emitter time, and is used when **Particle Orientation** is **Angular Velocity**.
property.particlefx.emitter-key-particle-blue = Initial Blue
property.particlefx.emitter-key-particle-blue.tooltip = Blue tint assigned when each particle spawns. It can vary randomly by **Spread** and follow a curve over the emitter's duration; the particle-life **Blue** curve multiplies it later.
property.particlefx.emitter-key-particle-green = Initial Green
property.particlefx.emitter-key-particle-green.tooltip = Green tint assigned when each particle spawns. It can vary randomly by **Spread** and follow a curve over the emitter's duration; the particle-life **Green** curve multiplies it later.
property.particlefx.emitter-key-particle-life-time = Particle Life Time
property.particlefx.emitter-key-particle-life-time.tooltip = Number of seconds each spawned particle lives. It can vary randomly by **Spread** for each particle and follow a curve over the emitter's duration.
property.particlefx.emitter-key-particle-red = Initial Red
property.particlefx.emitter-key-particle-red.tooltip = Red tint assigned when each particle spawns. It can vary randomly by **Spread** and follow a curve over the emitter's duration; the particle-life **Red** curve multiplies it later.
property.particlefx.emitter-key-particle-rotation = Initial Rotation
property.particlefx.emitter-key-particle-rotation.tooltip = Rotation in degrees assigned when each particle spawns. It can vary randomly by **Spread** and follow a curve over the emitter's duration.
property.particlefx.emitter-key-particle-size = Initial Size
property.particlefx.emitter-key-particle-size.tooltip = Base size assigned when each particle spawns. It can vary randomly by **Spread** and over emitter time, but is ignored when **Size Mode** is **Auto**.
property.particlefx.emitter-key-particle-speed = Initial Speed
property.particlefx.emitter-key-particle-speed.tooltip = Initial speed, in scene units per second, along the launch direction. It can vary randomly by **Spread** and follow a curve over the emitter's duration.
property.particlefx.emitter-key-particle-stretch-factor-x = Initial Stretch X
property.particlefx.emitter-key-particle-stretch-factor-x.tooltip = Initial horizontal stretch assigned when each particle spawns. It can vary randomly by **Spread** and over emitter time; the particle-life **Stretch X** curve adds to it.
property.particlefx.emitter-key-particle-stretch-factor-y = Initial Stretch Y
property.particlefx.emitter-key-particle-stretch-factor-y.tooltip = Initial vertical stretch assigned when each particle spawns. It can vary randomly by **Spread** and over emitter time; the particle-life **Stretch Y** curve adds to it.
property.particlefx.emitter-key-size-x = Emitter Size X
property.particlefx.emitter-key-size-x.tooltip = Width of a box or 2D cone, or diameter of a circle, sphere, or 3D cone. It can vary by **Spread** per particle and follow a curve over the emitter's duration.
property.particlefx.emitter-key-size-y = Emitter Size Y
property.particlefx.emitter-key-size-y.tooltip = Height of a box, 2D cone, or 3D cone; unused by circle and sphere emitters. It can vary by **Spread** per particle and over emitter time.
property.particlefx.emitter-key-size-z = Emitter Size Z
property.particlefx.emitter-key-size-z.tooltip = Depth of a box emitter; use `0` for a flat 2D rectangle. It can vary by **Spread** per particle and follow a curve over the emitter's duration.
property.particlefx.emitter-key-spawn-rate = Spawn Rate
property.particlefx.emitter-key-spawn-rate.tooltip = Number of particles emitted per second. It can follow a curve over the emitter's duration; **Spread** randomly offsets the rate for an emitter instance.
property.particlefx.magnitude = Magnitude
property.particlefx.magnitude.tooltip = Strength of the modifier, keyable over emitter time with random **Spread** per particle. Positive **Radial** values repel and negative values attract; the sign also reverses acceleration and vortex rotation. Positive drag slows particles.
property.particlefx.max-distance = Max Distance
property.particlefx.max-distance.tooltip = Maximum range of a **Radial** or **Vortex** modifier. Radial uses distance from the modifier position; Vortex uses perpendicular distance from its axis. Particles outside the range are unaffected.
property.particlefx.particle-key-alpha = Alpha
property.particlefx.particle-key-alpha.tooltip = Multiplies each particle's initial alpha over its normalized lifetime. Use a curve from `1` to `0` to fade particles out.
property.particlefx.particle-key-angular-velocity = Angular Velocity
property.particlefx.particle-key-angular-velocity.tooltip = Multiplies **Initial Angular Velocity** over each particle's normalized lifetime. Used when **Particle Orientation** is **Angular Velocity**.
property.particlefx.particle-key-blue = Blue
property.particlefx.particle-key-blue.tooltip = Multiplies each particle's initial blue tint over its normalized lifetime.
property.particlefx.particle-key-green = Green
property.particlefx.particle-key-green.tooltip = Multiplies each particle's initial green tint over its normalized lifetime.
property.particlefx.particle-key-red = Red
property.particlefx.particle-key-red.tooltip = Multiplies each particle's initial red tint over its normalized lifetime.
property.particlefx.particle-key-rotation = Rotation
property.particlefx.particle-key-rotation.tooltip = Rotation offset in degrees applied over each particle's normalized lifetime. It is added to **Initial Rotation** and is not used with **Angular Velocity** orientation.
property.particlefx.particle-key-scale = Scale
property.particlefx.particle-key-scale.tooltip = Scale multiplier applied over each particle's normalized lifetime. Shape the curve to grow or shrink particles as they age.
property.particlefx.particle-key-stretch-factor-x = Stretch X
property.particlefx.particle-key-stretch-factor-x.tooltip = Horizontal stretch added to **Initial Stretch X** over each particle's normalized lifetime.
property.particlefx.particle-key-stretch-factor-y = Stretch Y
property.particlefx.particle-key-stretch-factor-y.tooltip = Vertical stretch added to **Initial Stretch Y** over each particle's normalized lifetime. When **Stretch With Velocity** is enabled, particle speed also scales this stretch.

# Properties: sound

property.sound.sound = Sound
property.sound.sound.tooltip = The audio resource played by this component. Supported formats are WAV, Ogg Vorbis, and Ogg Opus; Opus playback requires its decoder to be included in the App Manifest.
property.sound.looping = Loop
property.sound.looping.tooltip = Repeat the sound after it reaches the end. **Loop Count** controls how many additional times it repeats; without looping, the sound plays once.
property.sound.loopcount = Loop Count
property.sound.loopcount.tooltip = The number of additional repetitions after the initial play. `0` loops until explicitly stopped, `1` plays twice in total, and the maximum is `127`.
property.sound.group = Group
property.sound.group.tooltip = The sound group used for shared mixing and gain control. Components with the same group can be adjusted together; an empty value uses the built-in `master` group.
property.sound.gain = Gain
property.sound.gain.tooltip = The component's volume multiplier. `1.0` is unity gain and `0` is silent; the final level also includes per-play, group, and master gain.
property.sound.pan = Pan
property.sound.pan.tooltip = Positions the sound in the stereo field. `-1` is fully left, `0` is centered, and `1` is fully right.
property.sound.speed = Speed
property.sound.speed.tooltip = The playback-rate multiplier. `1.0` is normal speed, `0.5` is half speed, and `2.0` is double speed; changing speed also changes pitch.

# Properties: sprite

property.sprite.default-animation = Default Animation
property.sprite.default-animation.tooltip = Image or flip-book animation shown when the sprite starts. Animation data comes from the first atlas or tile source; change it at runtime with `sprite.play_flipbook()`.
property.sprite.offset = Offset
property.sprite.offset.tooltip = Normalized starting position of the default animation, from `0` to `1`. Use different offsets to start partway through playback or desynchronize otherwise identical animated sprites.
property.sprite.playback-rate = Playback Rate
property.sprite.playback-rate.tooltip = Multiplier applied to the animation's configured speed. `1` plays at normal speed, `2` twice as fast, and `0` pauses playback; negative values are clamped to `0`.
property.sprite.size-mode = Size Mode
property.sprite.size-mode.tooltip = **Auto** uses the selected image or animation's dimensions. **Manual** enables a custom **Size** and allows Slice-9 resizing.
property.sprite.slice9 = Slice 9
property.sprite.slice9.tooltip = **Manual size only.** Pixel margins for the **Left**, **Top**, **Right**, and **Bottom** edges: corners keep their size while edges and the center stretch. Applied when **Size** changes, not when transform scale changes; the atlas image's **Sprite Trim Mode** must be **Off**.

# Properties: tile map

property.tile-map.layer.id.tooltip = The layer identifier used by tile map APIs such as `tilemap.get_tile()` and `tilemap.set_tile()`. It must be unique within the tile map.
property.tile-map.layer.visible = Visible
property.tile-map.layer.visible.tooltip = Controls whether this layer is rendered. If the tile map supplies shapes to a collision object, hidden layers are disabled for collision as well.
property.tile-map.layer.z = Z
property.tile-map.layer.z.tooltip = Local depth offset applied to every tile in this layer. With the default render setup, higher final Z values appear in front; values outside **-1 to 1** are not rendered. The tile map component, game object, and parent transforms contribute to the final Z.
property.tile-map.tile-source = Tile Source
property.tile-map.tile-source.tooltip = Tile source that provides the tile images and optional collision shapes used by this tile map.

# Properties: tile source

property.tile-source.animation.id.tooltip = The identifier used to select this flip-book animation in components and runtime animation APIs. It must be unique within the tile source.
property.tile-source.collision-group.id.tooltip = The name of the collision group assigned to selected tile shapes. It is used for collision filtering and reported in physics messages and events.
property.tile-source.collision = Collision
property.tile-source.collision.tooltip = An optional image whose non-transparent pixels generate a convex collision shape for each tile. It must match the visual source image's dimensions; assign generated shapes to collision groups in the Outline.
property.tile-source.end-tile = End Tile
property.tile-source.end-tile.tooltip = The last tile included in the animation. Tiles are numbered from `1` at the top-left, proceeding left-to-right and then downward; an end before the start wraps through the last tile back to tile `1`.
property.tile-source.extrude-borders = Extrude Borders
property.tile-source.extrude-borders.tooltip = The number of pixels by which each tile's edge colors are copied outward in the generated texture. This helps prevent neighboring tiles from bleeding into the tile when sampled near its edge.
property.tile-source.flip-horizontal = Flip Horizontal
property.tile-source.flip-horizontal.tooltip = Mirror every animation frame horizontally during playback.
property.tile-source.flip-vertical = Flip Vertical
property.tile-source.flip-vertical.tooltip = Mirror every animation frame vertically during playback.
property.tile-source.fps = FPS
property.tile-source.fps.tooltip = The animation playback speed in frames per second. Higher values display the tiles more quickly.
property.tile-source.inner-padding = Inner Padding
property.tile-source.inner-padding.tooltip = The number of empty pixels added around each tile in the generated runtime texture. This does not describe spacing already present in the source image.
property.tile-source.playback = Playback
property.tile-source.playback.tooltip = Choose whether the animation remains on its first tile, plays once, or loops, and whether frames run forward, backward, or ping-pong. **Once Ping Pong** stops after returning to the second frame to avoid repeating the first frame when animations are chained.
property.tile-source.sprite-trim-mode = Sprite Trim Mode
property.tile-source.sprite-trim-mode.tooltip = Approximate each tile's non-transparent area with a polygon using up to the selected number of vertices instead of rendering its full rectangle. This can reduce transparent overdraw, but cannot be used with slice-9 sprites.
property.tile-source.start-tile = Start Tile
property.tile-source.start-tile.tooltip = The first tile included in the animation. Tiles are numbered from `1` at the top-left, proceeding left-to-right and then downward.
property.tile-source.tile-height = Tile Height
property.tile-source.tile-height.tooltip = The height in pixels of each tile's image content, excluding margin and spacing.
property.tile-source.tile-margin = Tile Margin
property.tile-source.tile-margin.tooltip = The number of source-image pixels surrounding every side of each tile. Set this to match the margin already present around tiles in the source image.
property.tile-source.tile-spacing = Tile Spacing
property.tile-source.tile-spacing.tooltip = The additional source-image gap in pixels between neighboring tiles, excluding their margins. Set this to match the spacing already present in the source image.
property.tile-source.tile-width = Tile Width
property.tile-source.tile-width.tooltip = The width in pixels of each tile's image content, excluding margin and spacing.

