form.label.project.bootstrap = Bootstrap
form.help.project.bootstrap = Initial settings for the engine
form.label.project.bootstrap.main_collection = Main Collection
form.help.project.bootstrap.main_collection = Source `.collection` resource the engine loads and initializes when the application starts, for example `/main/main.collection`. Its game objects and components form the initial running world.
form.label.project.bootstrap.render = Render
form.help.project.bootstrap.render = Source `.render` resource loaded at startup, for example `/builtins/render/default.render`. It selects the render script and exposes its named materials, render targets, and compute programs.
form.label.project.bootstrap.debug_init_script = Debug Init Script
form.help.project.bootstrap.debug_init_script = Optional Lua module loaded before the main collection is initialized. It is intended for debugger tooling and runs only in non-release engine builds; release builds ignore it.

form.label.project.project = Project
form.help.project.project = General project settings
form.label.project.project.title = Title
form.help.project.project.title = The application's display name. It is used in window titles and platform bundle metadata, and must not be empty.
form.label.project.project.version = Version
form.help.project.project.version = The application's release version, embedded in platform bundle metadata.
form.label.project.project.publisher = Publisher
form.help.project.project.publisher = Name of the person or organization that publishes the application. Available at runtime as `project.publisher`.
form.label.project.project.developer = Developer
form.help.project.project.developer = Name of the person or organization that develops the application. Available at runtime as `project.developer`.
form.label.project.project.write_log = Write Log
form.help.project.project.write_log = **Deprecated.** Legacy switch for writing a log file to disk, retained for compatibility. Use **Write Log File** instead.
form.label.project.project.write_log_file = Write Log File
form.help.project.project.write_log_file = Controls when bundled applications write logs to disk: **Never**, **Debug** builds only, or **Always** for both Debug and Release builds. Runs launched from the editor still write debug logs with **Never**. The file is named `log.txt`, or `instance_N_log.txt` for additional editor instances.
form.label.project.project.minimum_log_level = Minimum Log Level
form.help.project.project.minimum_log_level = The lowest severity that will be logged. Messages below the selected level are suppressed; messages at that level and above are kept.
form.label.project.project.compress_archive = Compress Archive
form.help.project.project.compress_archive = Compresses the game archive when bundling. This has no effect on Android because the APK already stores the data compressed.
form.label.project.project.dependencies = Dependencies
form.help.project.project.dependencies = URLs of Defold library projects to import. Prefer URLs pinned to a specific release or commit so library updates do not unexpectedly break the project.
form.label.project.project.dependencies_metadata = Dependencies Metadata
form.help.project.project.dependencies_metadata = Includes library URL and revision metadata in the runtime bundle so crash reports can identify the exact dependency versions in use.
form.label.project.project.custom_resources = Custom Resources
form.help.project.project.custom_resources = Comma-separated files or directories to include in the main game archive. Directories are included recursively; load these files at runtime with `sys.load_resource()`.
form.label.project.project.bundle_resources = Bundle Resources
form.help.project.project.bundle_resources = Comma-separated absolute project directory paths starting with `/`, copied as-is into the application package outside the game archive. Each directory must contain platform, architecture-platform, or `common` subfolders.
form.label.project.project.bundle_exclude_resources = Bundle Exclude Resources
form.help.project.project.bundle_exclude_resources = Comma-separated resource paths to remove from the files collected by **Bundle Resources**, including bundle resources supplied by dependencies.

form.label.project.android = Android
form.help.project.android = Android related settings
form.label.project.android.app_icon_36x36 = App Icon 36x36
form.help.project.android.app_icon_36x36 = 36x36 PNG used as the launcher icon on **ldpi** devices (0.75x density). If unset, Defold scales the largest configured Android app icon, or its built-in icon.
form.label.project.android.app_icon_48x48 = App Icon 48x48
form.help.project.android.app_icon_48x48 = 48x48 PNG used as the launcher icon on **mdpi** devices (1x density). If unset, Defold scales the largest configured Android app icon, or its built-in icon.
form.label.project.android.app_icon_72x72 = App Icon 72x72
form.help.project.android.app_icon_72x72 = 72x72 PNG used as the launcher icon on **hdpi** devices (1.5x density). If unset, Defold scales the largest configured Android app icon, or its built-in icon.
form.label.project.android.app_icon_96x96 = App Icon 96x96
form.help.project.android.app_icon_96x96 = 96x96 PNG used as the launcher icon on **xhdpi** devices (2x density). If unset, Defold scales the largest configured Android app icon, or its built-in icon.
form.label.project.android.app_icon_144x144 = App Icon 144x144
form.help.project.android.app_icon_144x144 = 144x144 PNG used as the launcher icon on **xxhdpi** devices (3x density). If unset, Defold scales the largest configured Android app icon, or its built-in icon.
form.label.project.android.app_icon_192x192 = App Icon 192x192
form.help.project.android.app_icon_192x192 = 192x192 PNG used as the launcher icon on **xxxhdpi** devices (4x density). If unset, Defold scales the largest configured Android app icon, or its built-in icon.
form.label.project.android.push_icon_small = Push Icon Small
form.help.project.android.push_icon_small = Fallback PNG used as the small notification icon when no density-specific small icon matches. If no push icon is configured, notifications use the application icon.
form.label.project.android.push_icon_large = Push Icon Large
form.help.project.android.push_icon_large = Fallback PNG used as the large notification icon when no density-specific large icon matches. If no push icon is configured, notifications use the application icon.
form.label.project.android.push_icon_small_ldpi = Push Icon Small LDPI
form.help.project.android.push_icon_small_ldpi = PNG used as the small notification icon on **ldpi** devices (0.75x density). It overrides **Push Icon Small** for this density.
form.label.project.android.push_icon_small_mdpi = Push Icon Small MDPI
form.help.project.android.push_icon_small_mdpi = PNG used as the small notification icon on **mdpi** devices (1x density). It overrides **Push Icon Small** for this density.
form.label.project.android.push_icon_small_hdpi = Push Icon Small HDPI
form.help.project.android.push_icon_small_hdpi = PNG used as the small notification icon on **hdpi** devices (1.5x density). It overrides **Push Icon Small** for this density.
form.label.project.android.push_icon_small_xhdpi = Push Icon Small XHDPI
form.help.project.android.push_icon_small_xhdpi = PNG used as the small notification icon on **xhdpi** devices (2x density). It overrides **Push Icon Small** for this density.
form.label.project.android.push_icon_small_xxhdpi = Push Icon Small XXHDPI
form.help.project.android.push_icon_small_xxhdpi = PNG used as the small notification icon on **xxhdpi** devices (3x density). It overrides **Push Icon Small** for this density.
form.label.project.android.push_icon_small_xxxhdpi = Push Icon Small XXXHDPI
form.help.project.android.push_icon_small_xxxhdpi = PNG used as the small notification icon on **xxxhdpi** devices (4x density). It overrides **Push Icon Small** for this density.
form.label.project.android.push_icon_large_ldpi = Push Icon Large LDPI
form.help.project.android.push_icon_large_ldpi = PNG used as the large notification icon on **ldpi** devices (0.75x density). It overrides **Push Icon Large** for this density.
form.label.project.android.push_icon_large_mdpi = Push Icon Large MDPI
form.help.project.android.push_icon_large_mdpi = PNG used as the large notification icon on **mdpi** devices (1x density). It overrides **Push Icon Large** for this density.
form.label.project.android.push_icon_large_hdpi = Push Icon Large HDPI
form.help.project.android.push_icon_large_hdpi = PNG used as the large notification icon on **hdpi** devices (1.5x density). It overrides **Push Icon Large** for this density.
form.label.project.android.push_icon_large_xhdpi = Push Icon Large XHDPI
form.help.project.android.push_icon_large_xhdpi = PNG used as the large notification icon on **xhdpi** devices (2x density). It overrides **Push Icon Large** for this density.
form.label.project.android.push_icon_large_xxhdpi = Push Icon Large XXHDPI
form.help.project.android.push_icon_large_xxhdpi = PNG used as the large notification icon on **xxhdpi** devices (3x density). It overrides **Push Icon Large** for this density.
form.label.project.android.push_icon_large_xxxhdpi = Push Icon Large XXXHDPI
form.help.project.android.push_icon_large_xxxhdpi = PNG used as the large notification icon on **xxxhdpi** devices (4x density). It overrides **Push Icon Large** for this density.
form.label.project.android.push_field_title = Push Field Title
form.help.project.android.push_field_title = Name of the JSON payload field whose value becomes the notification title. Leave empty to use the application name.
form.label.project.android.push_field_text = Push Field Text
form.help.project.android.push_field_text = Name of the JSON payload field whose value becomes the notification body. Leave empty to read the body from the `alert` field.
form.label.project.android.version_code = Version Code
form.help.project.android.version_code = Android's internal integer release identifier, used to determine whether one package is newer than another. Increase it for every published update; users normally see **Project > Version** instead.
form.label.project.android.minimum_sdk_version = Minimum SDK Version
form.help.project.android.minimum_sdk_version = Lowest Android API level on which the application may be installed and run. Raising it allows newer APIs but excludes older devices. Minimum: `21`.
form.label.project.android.target_sdk_version = Target SDK Version
form.help.project.android.target_sdk_version = Android API level the application is designed and tested for. It affects platform compatibility behavior and store requirements, but does not exclude devices allowed by **Minimum SDK Version**.
form.label.project.android.package = Package
form.help.project.android.package = Stable, unique Android application ID, such as `com.example.game`. Use at least two dot-separated segments; each must start with a letter and contain only letters, digits, or underscores. Changing it after release creates a different application. Replace `com.example.todo` before release.
form.label.project.android.gcm_sender_id = GCM Sender ID
form.help.project.android.gcm_sender_id = Firebase Cloud Messaging sender ID used for push notifications. This is the numeric project identifier assigned by Firebase, not the Android package name. Leave empty when push messaging is not configured.
form.label.project.android.fcm_application_id = FCM Application ID
form.help.project.android.fcm_application_id = Firebase application ID for this Android app, used by Firebase Cloud Messaging. It identifies the registered Firebase app and is distinct from both the package name and sender ID. Leave empty when push messaging is not configured.
form.label.project.android.manifest = Manifest
form.help.project.android.manifest = Android manifest XML template used when bundling. A custom file replaces Defold's built-in base manifest, while native-extension fragments are still merged into it; maintain required entries when upgrading.
form.label.project.android.iap_provider = IAP Provider
form.help.project.android.iap_provider = Store backend used by the in-app purchase integration. Choose **GooglePlay** for Google Play or **Amazon** for the Amazon Appstore.
form.label.project.android.input_method = Input Method
form.help.project.android.input_method = How Android keyboard input reaches the engine. **KeyEvent** is the legacy method; **HiddenInputField** uses the newer hidden text-input path.
form.label.project.android.immersive_mode = Immersive Mode
form.help.project.android.immersive_mode = Hides Android's navigation and status bars so the application uses the full screen and receives touches throughout it.
form.label.project.android.display_cutout = Display Cutout
form.help.project.android.display_cutout = Allows fullscreen content to extend into display-cutout areas such as notches and camera holes. Android 15/API 35 and later may enforce this behavior. Use `window.get_safe_area()` to keep important UI inside safe-area insets.
form.label.project.android.debuggable = Debuggable
form.help.project.android.debuggable = Sets `android:debuggable` in the manifest, allowing tools such as Android Studio profilers and debuggers to inspect the application and its files. Leave disabled for release builds unless explicitly needed.
form.label.project.android.proguard = ProGuard Config
form.help.project.android.proguard = Custom `.pro` rules used when shrinking and obfuscating Java code in the Android build. Add keep rules for code accessed through reflection or JNI so it is not removed or renamed. Leave empty when no project-specific rules are needed.
form.label.project.android.extract_native_libs = Extract Native Libs
form.help.project.android.extract_native_libs = Controls whether Android extracts native libraries from the package at installation. When disabled, libraries remain uncompressed and load directly from the package; this is required for compatibility with devices using 16 KB memory pages.

form.label.project.html5 = HTML5
form.help.project.html5 = HTML5 related settings
form.label.project.html5.set_custom_heap_size = Set Custom Heap Size
form.help.project.html5.set_custom_heap_size = **Deprecated.** Leave this disabled and use **Heap Size** instead. When enabled it makes **Custom Heap Size** override **Heap Size**.
form.label.project.html5.custom_heap_size = Custom Heap Size
form.help.project.html5.custom_heap_size = **Deprecated.** When **Set Custom Heap Size** is enabled this byte count overrides **Heap Size**. Convert the value from bytes to MiB by dividing by `1048576`, then enter it in **Heap Size**.
form.label.project.html5.heap_size = Heap Size
form.help.project.html5.heap_size = Initial WebAssembly heap size in MiB. The heap may grow at runtime; a larger initial size can reduce growth overhead but reserves more memory initially. Allowed range: `32`–`4096`.
form.label.project.html5.htmlfile = .html Shell
form.help.project.html5.htmlfile = HTML template used to generate `index.html` and host the game canvas. It supports Defold's Mustache template tokens.
form.label.project.html5.cssfile = Custom .css
form.help.project.html5.cssfile = CSS template inlined into the generated `index.html` before the game loader. Custom HTML shells must include the `DEFOLD_CUSTOM_CSS_INLINE` token for this CSS to be inserted.
form.label.project.html5.splash_image = Splash Image
form.help.project.html5.splash_image = Image copied into the bundle for display while the game loads. Accepted extensions are `.gif`, `.jpg`, `.jpeg`, `.png`, `.svg`, `.webp`, and `.avif`. Custom CSS must consume the `DEFOLD_SPLASH_IMAGE` token to show it.
form.label.project.html5.archive_location_prefix = Archive Location Prefix
form.help.project.html5.archive_location_prefix = Prepended to every archive data file path at startup. Use a full URL to serve game data from another host; that host must allow the requests with CORS headers.
form.label.project.html5.archive_location_suffix = Archive Location Suffix
form.help.project.html5.archive_location_suffix = Appended to every archive data file path at startup. A query string such as `?v=2` can force a new cached version.
form.label.project.html5.engine_arguments = Engine Arguments
form.help.project.html5.engine_arguments = Comma-separated engine arguments passed at startup. Use `--config=section.key=value` to override a configuration value.
form.label.project.html5.wasm_streaming = Wasm Streaming
form.help.project.html5.wasm_streaming = Compiles WebAssembly while it downloads for faster startup and lower peak memory use. The server must send `.wasm` files as `application/wasm`. The loader falls back to ordinary loading if streaming fails.
form.label.project.html5.show_fullscreen_button = Show Fullscreen Button
form.help.project.html5.show_fullscreen_button = Shows the fullscreen control below the canvas in the built-in HTML shell. Custom shells can use this setting as a Mustache condition.
form.label.project.html5.show_made_with_defold = Show "Made With Defold"
form.help.project.html5.show_made_with_defold = Shows the **Made with Defold** attribution below the canvas in the built-in HTML shell. Custom shells can use this setting as a Mustache condition.
form.label.project.html5.show_console_banner = Show Console Banner
form.help.project.html5.show_console_banner = Prints the **Made with Defold** banner in the browser developer console when the engine starts.
form.label.project.html5.scale_mode = Scale Mode
form.help.project.html5.scale_mode = Controls canvas resizing. **Downscale Fit** preserves aspect ratio and only shrinks. **Fit** preserves aspect ratio and can shrink or grow. **Stretch** fills the page and may distort. **No Scale** keeps the configured display dimensions.
form.label.project.html5.retry_count = Retry Count
form.help.project.html5.retry_count = Number of retries after a network error while loading bundle files. The initial request is separate.
form.label.project.html5.retry_time = Retry Time
form.help.project.html5.retry_time = Delay in seconds before retrying a bundle file after a network error.
form.label.project.html5.transparent_graphics_context = Transparent Context
form.help.project.html5.transparent_graphics_context = Requests an alpha channel for the HTML5 graphics context so the page can show through transparent canvas pixels. The game must also render transparent pixels.

form.label.project.ios = iOS
form.help.project.ios = iOS related settings
form.label.project.ios.app_icon_76x76 = App Icon 76x76
form.help.project.ios.app_icon_76x76 = Square **76 × 76 px PNG** used for the iPad home-screen icon. If omitted, Defold scales the largest configured iOS icon — or its built-in icon — to this size.
form.label.project.ios.app_icon_120x120 = App Icon 120x120
form.help.project.ios.app_icon_120x120 = Square **120 × 120 px PNG** used for the 2× iPhone home-screen icon. If omitted, Defold scales the largest configured iOS icon — or its built-in icon — to this size.
form.label.project.ios.app_icon_152x152 = App Icon 152x152
form.help.project.ios.app_icon_152x152 = Square **152 × 152 px PNG** used for the 2× iPad home-screen icon. If omitted, Defold scales the largest configured iOS icon — or its built-in icon — to this size.
form.label.project.ios.app_icon_167x167 = App Icon 167x167
form.help.project.ios.app_icon_167x167 = Square **167 × 167 px PNG** used for the 2× iPad Pro home-screen icon. If omitted, Defold scales the largest configured iOS icon — or its built-in icon — to this size.
form.label.project.ios.app_icon_180x180 = App Icon 180x180
form.help.project.ios.app_icon_180x180 = Square **180 × 180 px PNG** used for the 3× iPhone home-screen icon. If omitted, Defold scales the largest configured iOS icon — or its built-in icon — to this size.
form.label.project.ios.icons_asset = Icons Asset
form.help.project.ios.icons_asset = Compiled Xcode icon catalog (`Assets.car`) containing the complete iOS icon set, including the App Store icon. Build it for a generic iOS device; Defold copies it into the application bundle.
form.label.project.ios.launch_screen = Launch Screen
form.help.project.ios.launch_screen = Compiled Xcode launch-screen directory (`.storyboardc`), not the source `.storyboard`. Add any images it references through **Bundle Resources**.
form.label.project.ios.pre_renderered_icons = Pre Renderered Icons
form.help.project.ios.pre_renderered_icons = Controls the legacy `UIPrerenderedIcon` metadata. On iOS 6 and earlier, enable this for finished icon artwork to prevent an automatic glossy highlight.
form.label.project.ios.bundle_identifier = Bundle Identifier
form.help.project.ios.bundle_identifier = Unique identifier registered with Apple that must match the App ID and provisioning profile. Use at least two dot-separated segments; each must start with an ASCII letter and contain only letters, digits, `_`, or `-`. `example.unnamed` must be changed for distribution.
form.label.project.ios.bundle_name = Bundle Name
form.help.project.ios.bundle_name = Short internal application name written to `CFBundleName`; maximum **15 characters**.
form.label.project.ios.bundle_version = Bundle Version
form.help.project.ios.bundle_version = Build number written to `CFBundleVersion`. Use a number or `x.y.z` and increase it for each uploaded build. If empty, Defold uses the project version.
form.label.project.ios.infoplist = Info.plist
form.help.project.ios.infoplist = Base `Info.plist` template for the bundle, replacing Defold's built-in template. Native-extension fragments are still merged into the custom base. Preserve its conditional Bonjour and local-network entries if non-release builds need target discovery, profiling, hot reload, or log streaming.
form.label.project.ios.privacymanifest = PrivacyInfo.xcprivacy
form.help.project.ios.privacymanifest = Apple privacy manifest declaring collected data and required-reason API use. During bundling it is merged with privacy manifests from project dependencies.
form.label.project.ios.entitlements = Custom entitlements
form.help.project.ios.entitlements = Property-list file merged into the signing entitlements from the provisioning profile. Every custom key must already exist in the profile; supplied values replace its values, including wildcards.
form.label.project.ios.default_language = Default Language
form.help.project.ios.default_language = Fallback language used when the user's preferred language is absent from **Localizations** (`CFBundleDevelopmentRegion`). Use a two-letter ISO 639-1 code when available, otherwise a three-letter ISO 639-2 code.
form.label.project.ios.localizations = Localizations
form.help.project.ios.localizations = Comma-separated language names or ISO language codes supported by the application (`CFBundleLocalizations`). Include every language handled manually; iOS will not report an omitted language through `sys.get_sys_info()`.

form.label.project.osx = OSX
form.help.project.osx = Mac OSX related settings
form.label.project.osx.app_icon = App Icon
form.help.project.osx.app_icon = macOS application icon in `.icns` format. During bundling it is copied into the app as `Contents/Resources/icon.icns`.
form.label.project.osx.bundle_identifier = Bundle Identifier
form.help.project.osx.bundle_identifier = Unique identifier macOS uses to identify the app and its updates (`CFBundleIdentifier`). Use at least two dot-separated segments; each must start with a letter and contain only letters, digits, `_`, or `-`. `example.unnamed` must be changed for distribution.
form.label.project.osx.bundle_name = Bundle Name
form.help.project.osx.bundle_name = Short internal bundle name stored as `CFBundleName`. It is limited to 15 characters.
form.label.project.osx.bundle_version = Bundle Version
form.help.project.osx.bundle_version = Build number stored as `CFBundleVersion`, used to distinguish app builds. Enter a number or a dotted version such as `1.2.3`.
form.label.project.osx.infoplist = Info.plist
form.help.project.osx.infoplist = The `Info.plist` template that describes the macOS app bundle. A custom template replaces Defold's built-in base template, while native-extension manifest fragments are still merged into it.
form.label.project.osx.privacymanifest = PrivacyInfo.xcprivacy
form.help.project.osx.privacymanifest = Declares the data your app collects and the required-reason APIs it uses. Defold merges this `.xcprivacy` file with privacy manifests from dependencies and places the result in `Contents/Resources`.
form.label.project.osx.default_language = Default Language
form.help.project.osx.default_language = Fallback language and region (`CFBundleDevelopmentRegion`) used when the user's preferred language is not listed in **Localizations**. Use a two-letter ISO 639-1 code when available, otherwise a three-letter ISO 639-2 code.
form.label.project.osx.localizations = Localizations
form.help.project.osx.localizations = Comma-separated language names or ISO language codes that your app handles (`CFBundleLocalizations`), for example `en, sv, ja`. macOS uses this list when choosing the user's preferred localization.

form.label.project.windows = Windows
form.help.project.windows = Windows related settings
form.label.project.windows.app_icon = App Icon
form.help.project.windows.app_icon = Uncompressed 32-bit `.ico` file embedded in the bundled executable. It must contain exact `16`, `24`, `32`, `48`, `64`, `96`, `128`, and `256` px square images to replace every Defold icon size. If unset, the executable keeps the default icon.

form.label.project.collection = Collection
form.help.project.collection = Collection related settings
form.label.project.collection.max_instances = Max Instances
form.help.project.collection.max_instances = Maximum game objects alive in each collection, including placed objects, spawned objects, and objects awaiting end-of-frame deletion. At capacity, creation fails and the engine emits a buffer-full message. Higher values reserve more memory, though builds may allocate a smaller safe capacity when all contents are known.
form.label.project.collection.max_input_stack_entries = Max Input Stack Entries
form.help.project.collection.max_input_stack_entries = Maximum game objects in each collection that may hold input focus at once. One game object uses one entry even with several input-capable components; reacquiring focus moves it to the top. At capacity, another object cannot acquire focus. Higher limits reserve more memory.

form.label.project.collectionfactory = Collection Factory
form.help.project.collectionfactory = Collection factory related settings
form.label.project.collectionfactory.max_count = Max Count
form.help.project.collectionfactory.max_count = Configured maximum number of collection factory components in one loaded collection. Runtime capacity is bounded by both this maximum and the exact build-time count; dynamic prototypes make the configured maximum especially important. Reaching capacity prevents additional components from being created; unnecessarily high values can reserve more memory.

form.label.project.collection_proxy = Collection Proxy
form.help.project.collection_proxy = Collection proxy related settings
form.label.project.collection_proxy.max_count = Max Count
form.help.project.collection_proxy.max_count = Maximum number of collection proxy components in one loaded collection, whether or not their target collections are loaded. Defold preallocates this component capacity when an exact build-time count is unavailable; values that are too low prevent additional proxies from being created and log an error, while unnecessarily high values use more memory.

form.label.project.factory = Factory
form.help.project.factory = Game object factory related settings
form.label.project.factory.max_count = Max Count
form.help.project.factory.max_count = Maximum Factory components in one loaded collection, not the game objects they spawn. Runtime capacity also accounts for the exact build-time count; dynamic prototypes require the configured maximum. At capacity, loading or spawning the game object that contains another Factory component fails. Unnecessarily high values use more memory only when exact build-time counting does not determine the capacity.

form.label.project.gui = GUI
form.help.project.gui = GUI related settings
form.label.project.gui.max_count = Max Count
form.help.project.gui.max_count = Maximum number of GUI components in a loaded collection. Exceeding the capacity prevents additional GUI components from being created. Increasing it can reserve more memory when build-time exact counting cannot determine the required capacity.
form.label.project.gui.max_animation_count = Max Animation Count
form.help.project.gui.max_animation_count = Maximum number of simultaneously active animations in each GUI scene. This capacity is preallocated for every scene; when it is full, additional animations do not start.
form.label.project.gui.max_particle_count = Max Particle Count
form.help.project.gui.max_particle_count = Maximum number of GUI particles rendered in each GUI scene. Particles beyond the limit still simulate but are not rendered. The vertex buffer grows with actual use up to this limit, so rendering more particles uses more graphics memory.
form.label.project.gui.max_particlefx_count = Max ParticleFX Count
form.help.project.gui.max_particlefx_count = Maximum number of simultaneously playing GUI ParticleFX instances in a loaded collection. The engine preallocates this capacity; when it is full, additional play requests are disregarded.
form.label.project.gui.safe_area_mode = Safe Area Mode
form.help.project.gui.safe_area_mode = Controls how GUI adjustment uses safe-area insets on Android and iOS. **None** ignores them; **Long Side** uses left/right in landscape and top/bottom in portrait; **Short Side** uses the opposite pair; **Both Sides** uses all four. Platforms without insets use the full window, and scripts can override the mode per GUI scene.

form.label.project.label = Label
form.help.project.label = Label related settings
form.label.project.label.max_count = Max Count
form.help.project.label.max_count = **Maximum number of label components in each loaded collection.** Creating a label beyond the capacity fails and logs an error. Higher values reserve more memory only when build-time exact counting cannot determine the required capacity.
form.label.project.label.subpixels = Subpixels
form.help.project.label.subpixels = Controls whether labels may render at fractional positions. When disabled, each label's world-space X and Y position is truncated to whole units before camera projection, which helps pixel-aligned text but does not compensate for fractional camera movement.
form.label.project.light.max_count = Max Count
form.help.project.light.max_count = Maximum light-component capacity per loaded collection and maximum non-ambient light render instances across loaded collections. Ambient lights count only toward their collection's component capacity. Higher values reserve component and render-buffer capacity; creating a light when capacity is full fails.

form.label.project.mesh = Mesh
form.help.project.mesh = Mesh related settings
form.label.project.mesh.max_count = Max Count
form.help.project.mesh.max_count = Maximum number of mesh components per loaded collection. When build-time analysis cannot determine an exact count, Defold preallocates storage from this limit; higher values can use more memory. Creating a mesh when the capacity is full fails and logs an error.

form.label.project.model = Model
form.help.project.model = Model related settings
form.label.project.model.max_count = Max Count
form.help.project.model.max_count = Maximum number of Model components in one loaded collection. Defold preallocates this capacity when dynamic factory content prevents exact build-time counting; a value that is too low prevents additional components, while an unnecessarily high value uses more memory.
form.label.project.model.split_meshes = Split Meshes
form.help.project.model.split_meshes = When enabled, splits imported meshes as needed to fit 16-bit vertex indices into smaller meshes at build time. This improves compatibility with constrained graphics targets, but the extra mesh parts can increase draw calls.
form.label.project.model.max_bone_matrix_texture_width = Max Bone Matrix Tex Width
form.help.project.model.max_bone_matrix_texture_width = Maximum width, in pixels, of the per-collection **RGBA32F** texture that stores bone matrices for GPU-skinned Model components. The texture grows only as needed, up to this value and the GPU limit; raise either dimension after a cache-too-small warning, noting that larger actual textures use more memory.
form.label.project.model.max_bone_matrix_texture_height = Max Bone Matrix Tex Height
form.help.project.model.max_bone_matrix_texture_height = Maximum height, in pixels, of the per-collection **RGBA32F** texture that stores bone matrices for GPU-skinned Model components. The texture grows only as needed, up to this value and the GPU limit; raise either dimension after a cache-too-small warning, noting that larger actual textures use more memory.
form.label.project.model.max_morph_target_texture_width = Max Morph Target Tex Width
form.help.project.model.max_morph_target_texture_width = Maximum width, in pixels, of each generated morph-target texture array. Use a power-of-two limit. The computed layout must fit both configured dimensions and the target GPU's maximum texture size; otherwise the model cannot be built or loaded.
form.label.project.model.max_morph_target_texture_height = Max Morph Target Tex Height
form.help.project.model.max_morph_target_texture_height = Maximum height, in pixels, of each generated morph-target texture array. Use a power-of-two limit. The computed layout must fit both configured dimensions and the target GPU's maximum texture size; otherwise the model cannot be built or loaded.

form.label.project.particle_fx = ParticleFX
form.help.project.particle_fx = ParticleFX related settings
form.label.project.particle_fx.max_particle_count = Max Particle Count
form.help.project.particle_fx.max_particle_count = Maximum total number of ParticleFX particles rendered in each loaded collection. Particles beyond the limit are not rendered and produce a warning. GPU memory grows with the amount of particle data actually rendered, up to this limit. An emitter's own **Max Particle Count** separately limits how many particles it creates.
form.label.project.particle_fx.max_particle_buffer_count = Max Particle Buffer Count
form.help.project.particle_fx.max_particle_buffer_count = Per-collection scratch capacity for particles converted to vertex data before each GPU upload, capped by **Max Particle Count**. Lower values reduce the CPU scratch buffer but can require more uploads; this does not limit the total number of living particles.
form.label.project.particle_fx.max_count = Max Count
form.help.project.particle_fx.max_count = Maximum number of ParticleFX components and concurrent effect instances in each loaded collection. When full, another component or instance cannot be created. Increasing it uses more memory when build-time exact counting cannot determine the required component capacity.
form.label.project.particle_fx.max_emitter_count = Max Emitter Count
form.help.project.particle_fx.max_emitter_count = Maximum total number of emitters across all concurrent ParticleFX instances in each loaded collection. A single effect can contain multiple emitters. If the limit is exceeded, the collection's entire ParticleFX render pass is skipped and a warning is logged.

form.label.project.script = Script
form.help.project.script = Script system settings
form.label.project.script.shared_state = Shared State
form.help.project.script.shared_state = Controls whether game object scripts, GUI scripts, and the render script use one Lua state. Globals and loaded-module caches are shared when enabled and isolated when disabled. A shared state uses less memory and is required by the Editor debugger.

form.label.project.sound = Sound
form.help.project.sound = Sound related settings
form.label.project.sound.gain = Gain
form.help.project.sound.gain = Master gain applied to all sound output. `0` is silent and `1` is unity gain.
form.label.project.sound.use_linear_gain = Use Linear Gain
form.help.project.sound.use_linear_gain = Controls how gain values are mixed. When enabled, master, group, component, and instance gains are multiplied linearly; when disabled, an exponential curve makes `0.5` sound approximately half as loud. The optional OpenAL backend always uses linear gain.
form.label.project.sound.max_sound_data = Max Sound Data
form.help.project.sound.max_sound_data = Maximum number of unique sound resources that can be loaded at once. Increase it if the engine reports that it is out of sound data slots; higher values reserve more memory.
form.label.project.sound.max_sound_buffers = Max Sound Buffers
form.help.project.sound.max_sound_buffers = Buffering budget used by the **OpenAL** sound backend. OpenAL automatically raises values below twice **Max Sound Sources** to that minimum. Higher values increase queued audio and memory use; other backends ignore this setting.
form.label.project.sound.max_sound_sources = Max Sound Sources
form.help.project.sound.max_sound_sources = Maximum number of sounds the **OpenAL** backend can output concurrently. Starting another sound fails while all sources are in use; higher values also require more buffers and memory. Other sound backends ignore this setting.
form.label.project.sound.max_sound_instances = Max Sound Instances
form.help.project.sound.max_sound_instances = Maximum number of sound instances, or voices, that may exist at once. Each call that starts a sound creates an instance; playback fails when the limit is reached. Higher values reserve more memory.
form.label.project.sound.max_component_count = Max Component Count
form.help.project.sound.max_component_count = Maximum number of sound components in each collection. Increase it when a collection contains more sound components; higher values reserve more component memory.
form.label.project.sound.sample_frame_count = Sample Frame Count
form.help.project.sound.sample_frame_count = Fallback number of sample frames processed per audio update. A buffer size reported by the audio device takes precedence; otherwise `0` selects `1024` at 48 kHz or `768` at 44.1 kHz. OpenAL uses this only for its streamed output buffer.
form.label.project.sound.use_thread = Use Thread
form.help.project.sound.use_thread = Runs sound playback updates on a separate thread, reducing the risk of audio stutter when the main thread is busy. Platforms without thread support always update sound on the main thread.
form.label.project.sound.stream_enabled = Stream Enabled
form.help.project.sound.stream_enabled = Loads sound files from the resource archive in chunks instead of keeping each complete file in memory. This reduces runtime memory and initial loading at the cost of ongoing I/O and careful cache sizing.
form.label.project.sound.stream_chunk_size = Stream Chunk Size
form.help.project.sound.stream_chunk_size = Number of bytes loaded for each subsequent chunk of a streamed sound. Smaller chunks use the shared cache more efficiently when many sounds are loaded but increase I/O overhead. Whether a sound is fully loaded depends on **Stream Preload Size**, not this chunk size.
form.label.project.sound.stream_preload_size = Stream Preload Size
form.help.project.sound.stream_preload_size = Number of bytes initially loaded from each streamed sound in the resource archive. This initial chunk cannot be evicted and remains in the cache while the sound resource is loaded, so larger values increase persistent memory use.
form.label.project.sound.stream_cache_size = Stream Cache Size
form.help.project.sound.stream_cache_size = Total byte budget shared by streamed sound chunks, including each loaded sound's non-evictable preload chunk. Size it for all retained preloads plus working stream chunks; otherwise evictable chunks may churn and playback can fail.

form.label.project.sprite = Sprite
form.help.project.sprite = Sprite related settings
form.label.project.sprite.max_count = Max Count
form.help.project.sprite.max_count = **Maximum number of sprite components in a loaded collection.** Exceeding the capacity prevents additional components from being created. Higher values reserve more memory only when build-time exact counting cannot determine the required capacity.
form.label.project.sprite.subpixels = Subpixels
form.help.project.sprite.subpixels = Controls whether sprites may render at fractional positions. When disabled, each sprite's world-space translation is truncated to whole units before projection. This can help pixel art but does not guarantee screen-pixel snapping when the camera or projection is fractional.

form.label.project.tilemap = Tilemap
form.help.project.tilemap = Tilemap related settings
form.label.project.tilemap.max_count = Max Count
form.help.project.tilemap.max_count = Maximum number of tile map components that may exist at once in a loaded collection. Reaching the limit prevents additional components from being created. Defold preallocates component storage from this capacity when it cannot derive an exact count at build time, so avoid setting it unnecessarily high.
form.label.project.tilemap.max_tile_count = Max Tile Count
form.help.project.tilemap.max_tile_count = Maximum total number of visible tiles that all tile maps in a collection can submit for rendering at once. Tiles beyond the limit are omitted and an error is logged. The renderer preallocates a vertex buffer for this capacity, so higher values use more memory.

form.label.project.box2d = Box2D
form.help.project.box2d = Box2D physics settings. Availability of options depends on the Box2D version.
form.label.project.box2d.velocity_iterations = Velocity Iterations
form.help.project.box2d.velocity_iterations = Number of velocity-solver iterations per physics step in **Box2D 2.2**. Higher values improve the accuracy of contacts, friction, restitution, and joints, but use more CPU; lower values improve performance at the cost of stability.
form.label.project.box2d.position_iterations = Position Iterations
form.help.project.box2d.position_iterations = Number of position-solver iterations per physics step in **Box2D 2.2**. Higher values reduce overlap and joint-position error, but use more CPU; lower values improve performance at the cost of positional accuracy.
form.label.project.box2d.sub_step_count = Sub Step Count
form.help.project.box2d.sub_step_count = Number of sub-steps used for each physics step in **Box2D 3.x**. Higher values improve collision and joint stability, especially for fast-moving bodies, but use more CPU; lower values improve performance at the cost of accuracy.

form.label.project.display = Display
form.help.project.display = Resolution and other display related settings
form.label.project.display.width = Width
form.help.project.display.width = Width of the application window in pixels and the default logical rendering width.
form.label.project.display.height = Height
form.help.project.display.height = Height of the application window in pixels and the default logical rendering height.
form.label.project.display.high_dpi = High DPI
form.help.project.display.high_dpi = Creates a higher-resolution back buffer on supported displays for sharper graphics. **Width** and **Height** remain the logical resolution used by scripts and properties.
form.label.project.display.samples = Samples
form.help.project.display.samples = Number of anti-aliasing samples used to smooth rendered edges. `0` disables anti-aliasing.
form.label.project.display.fullscreen = Fullscreen
form.help.project.display.fullscreen = Starts the application fullscreen instead of in a window. The exact fullscreen mode, including whether it is borderless, depends on the desktop platform and graphics backend.
form.label.project.display.display_profiles = Display Profiles
form.help.project.display.display_profiles = Display Profiles resource used to select matching GUI layouts for different screen sizes, orientations, and device models.
form.label.project.display.dynamic_orientation = Dynamic Orientation
form.help.project.display.dynamic_orientation = Allows Android and iOS builds to use both portrait and landscape orientations and switch when the device rotates. When disabled, the supported orientation is inferred from **Width** and **Height**. The development app does not currently respect this setting.
form.label.project.display.update_frequency = Update Frequency
form.help.project.display.update_frequency = Desired game-loop and rendering rate in hertz. `0` uses a variable frame rate; a positive value such as `30` caps the rate when the device can run that fast.
form.label.project.display.swap_interval = Swap Interval
form.help.project.display.swap_interval = Requests presentation relative to the display refresh. `0` disables vertical sync and `1` presents every refresh. Larger values may skip intervals on OpenGL, while Vulkan and Metal treat any nonzero value as enabling vertical sync. Actual behavior depends on the backend and driver.
form.label.project.display.vsync = Vsync
form.help.project.display.vsync = **Deprecated compatibility setting.** When disabled, it forces the effective **Swap Interval** to `0`; when enabled, **Swap Interval** determines the behavior. Use **Swap Interval** for new projects.
form.label.project.display.variable_dt = Variable DT
form.help.project.display.variable_dt = **Deprecated.** Enabling this maps the built project to **Vsync** disabled and **Update Frequency** set to `0`, reproducing the old variable-timestep behavior.
form.label.project.display.display_device_info = Display Device Info
form.help.project.display.display_device_info = Logs graphics device details at startup. The available fields and level of detail vary significantly by graphics backend, driver, and platform. Useful when diagnosing graphics problems.

form.label.project.engine = Engine
form.help.project.engine = Runtime settings for the engine
form.label.project.engine.run_while_iconified = Run While Iconified
form.help.project.engine.run_while_iconified = Keeps updates and sound running while the application window is minimized; rendering remains paused. When disabled, updates and sound also pause until the window is restored. Desktop platforms only.
form.label.project.engine.fixed_update_frequency = Fixed Update Frequency
form.help.project.engine.fixed_update_frequency = Sets the frequency of fixed updates in Hz. This controls `fixed_update(self, dt)` and physics when **Use Fixed Timestep** is enabled. `0` disables fixed updates.
form.label.project.engine.max_time_step = Max Time Step
form.help.project.engine.max_time_step = Caps the `dt` passed to regular update callbacks after a slow or suspended frame. It does not cap the fixed `dt` passed to `fixed_update()`; excess elapsed time is discarded.

form.label.project.font = Font
form.help.project.font = Font related settings
form.label.project.font.runtime_generation = Runtime Generation
form.help.project.font.runtime_generation = Generates TrueType glyphs on demand instead of baking them into textures. Applies to **Distance Field** fonts with a compatible material; runtime font collections can add further TTF sources. Target builds require **Use Full Text Layout System** in the App Manifest. Put representative shaped text in **Characters** to prewarm common glyphs. This can reduce bundle size and runtime memory.

form.label.project.graphics = Graphics
form.help.project.graphics = Graphics related settings
form.label.project.graphics.default_texture_min_filter = Default Texture Min Filter
form.help.project.graphics.default_texture_min_filter = Sets the project minification filter used when a material sampler does not override its filter. `nearest` preserves hard pixel edges, `linear` smooths them, and the mipmap modes also control filtering between mip levels.
form.label.project.graphics.default_texture_mag_filter = Default Texture Mag Filter
form.help.project.graphics.default_texture_mag_filter = Sets the project magnification filter used when a material sampler does not override its filter. `nearest` preserves hard pixel edges; `linear` produces a smoother result.
form.label.project.graphics.max_draw_calls = Max Draw Calls
form.help.project.graphics.max_draw_calls = Maximum number of draw calls that can be submitted per frame. If this capacity is exceeded, some objects are not rendered and a warning is logged. Increase it when that warning occurs, at the cost of more preallocated memory.
form.label.project.graphics.max_characters = Max Characters
form.help.project.graphics.max_characters = Capacity reserved for text-rendering data per frame, not a literal visible-character count. UTF-8 text and multi-layer fonts can consume multiple entries per displayed character. Text beyond the capacity is omitted and a warning is logged.
form.label.project.graphics.max_font_batches = Max Font Batches
form.help.project.graphics.max_font_batches = Maximum number of text batches that can be rendered per frame. Additional batches are not rendered when the capacity is reached, and a warning is logged. Increase it when that warning occurs, at the cost of more preallocated memory.
form.label.project.graphics.max_debug_vertices = Max Debug Vertices
form.help.project.graphics.max_debug_vertices = Number of vertices reserved for debug rendering, including physics shapes. Debug geometry beyond this capacity is omitted and a warning is logged. The setting is ignored in release builds.
form.label.project.graphics.texture_profiles = Texture Profiles
form.help.project.graphics.texture_profiles = Texture profiles file used when building texture resources. Its ordered path rules select compression format, mipmap generation, and maximum texture size for each resource.
form.label.project.graphics.verify_graphics_calls = Verify Graphics Calls
form.help.project.graphics.verify_graphics_calls = Enables backend-specific graphics API error checks in debug builds. A detected error normally triggers an assertion or debugger break and may also be logged. The checks can reduce performance and are not equally available on every backend.
form.label.project.graphics.opengl_version_hint = OpenGL Version Hint
form.help.project.graphics.opengl_version_hint = Requests the minimum desktop OpenGL version when creating the graphics context. It does not affect OpenGL ES; **Highest version available** lets the platform choose the best supported version. Requesting an unsupported version can prevent startup.
form.label.project.graphics.opengl_core_profile_hint = OpenGL Core Profile Hint
form.help.project.graphics.opengl_core_profile_hint = Requests a desktop OpenGL core-profile context, which excludes deprecated features such as immediate-mode rendering. Disable it only when native graphics code requires compatibility-profile features. It does not affect OpenGL ES.
form.label.project.graphics.vulkan_version_major = Vulkan Version Major
form.help.project.graphics.vulkan_version_major = Major part of the requested Vulkan API version. It is combined with **Vulkan Version Minor** and used only with the Vulkan backend. Requesting an unsupported version can prevent startup.
form.label.project.graphics.vulkan_version_minor = Vulkan Version Minor
form.help.project.graphics.vulkan_version_minor = Minor part of the requested Vulkan API version. It is combined with **Vulkan Version Major** and used only with the Vulkan backend. Requesting an unsupported version can prevent startup.
form.label.project.graphics.memory_size = Memory Size
form.help.project.graphics.memory_size = Maximum memory, in MB, that the graphics driver may use on Nintendo Switch. `0` uses the platform default with no explicit limit.

form.label.project.input = Input
form.help.project.input = Input related settings
form.label.project.input.repeat_delay = Repeat Delay
form.help.project.input.repeat_delay = **Seconds** before a held action with a positive value first sets `action.repeated`. Applies project-wide, including to suitable analog actions rather than only digital inputs.
form.label.project.input.repeat_interval = Repeat Interval
form.help.project.input.repeat_interval = **Seconds** between subsequent `action.repeated` events while an action has a positive held value. Applies project-wide, including to suitable analog actions rather than only digital inputs.
form.label.project.input.gamepads = Gamepads
form.help.project.input.gamepads = Legacy `.gamepads` mappings that translate device-specific buttons and axes into standard gamepad inputs. They provide device-name fallback mappings when no SDL GUID mapping matches.
form.label.project.input.gamepad_database = Gamepad Database
form.help.project.input.gamepad_database = An SDL `gamecontrollerdb.txt` file that maps controller GUIDs and layouts to standard gamepad inputs. GUID mappings take priority over legacy device-name mappings.
form.label.project.input.gamepad_deadzone = Gamepad Dead Zone
form.help.project.input.gamepad_deadzone = Normalized radial dead-zone threshold for analog sticks mapped by the SDL gamepad database. Stick vectors at or below this magnitude become zero; legacy `.gamepads` mappings use their own dead zone.
form.label.project.input.game_binding = Game Binding
form.help.project.input.game_binding = The project-wide input binding resource that translates raw keyboard, mouse, touch, gamepad, and text input into named actions delivered to scripts and GUI scripts with input focus.
form.label.project.input.use_accelerometer = Use Accelerometer
form.help.project.input.use_accelerometer = Enables per-frame accelerometer input in native Android and iOS apps, exposed as `action.acc_x`, `action.acc_y`, and `action.acc_z`. Disable it when unused to reduce input processing and battery use.

form.label.project.network = Network
form.help.project.network = Network related settings
form.label.project.network.http_timeout = HTTP Timeout
form.help.project.network.http_timeout = Default timeout in seconds for `http.request()` when its options do not specify one. `0` waits indefinitely; a positive value prevents stalled requests from remaining active, but a value too low can fail on slow networks.
form.label.project.network.ssl_certificates = SSL Certificates
form.help.project.network.ssl_certificates = PEM file containing trusted CA certificates or self-signed certificate trust anchors, not bare public keys. Native targets use it for certificate-chain verification; HTML5 uses the browser's trust store. A CA bundle is available at `/builtins/ca-certificates/cacert.pem`.
form.label.project.network.http_thread_count = HTTP Thread Count
form.help.project.network.http_thread_count = Number of worker threads servicing native HTTP requests. `0` uses one thread and values above `15` are capped; Nintendo Switch caps the value at `2`. HTML5 ignores this setting. More threads can improve parallel throughput but use additional memory and CPU.
form.label.project.network.http_cache_enabled = HTTP Cache Enabled
form.help.project.network.http_cache_enabled = Enables the native on-disk cache for eligible `http.request()` responses and HTTP-loaded resources, reusing or revalidating them with HTTP cache headers. HTML5 uses the browser cache instead. Disable it when native responses must not persist.

form.label.project.physics = Physics
form.help.project.physics = Physics settings
form.label.project.physics.max_collision_object_count = Max Collision Object Count
form.help.project.physics.max_collision_object_count = Maximum number of collision-object components available in each physics world. Increase this if runtime spawning can exceed the limit; higher values reserve more memory.
form.label.project.physics.type = Type
form.help.project.physics.type = Selects the physics engine and dimensionality: **2D** uses Box2D, while **3D** uses Bullet. This affects supported shapes, joints, and simulation behavior.
form.label.project.physics.use_fixed_timestep = Use Fixed Timestep
form.help.project.physics.use_fixed_timestep = Updates physics at a fixed, frame-rate-independent interval for a more stable simulation. Use `fixed_update(self, dt)` for physics-related script logic; **Fixed Update Frequency** controls the interval. Recommended for new projects.
form.label.project.physics.debug = Debug
form.help.project.physics.debug = Draws available collision shapes, joints, and contact diagnostics in debug builds. Release builds ignore it, and the diagnostics provided depend on the selected physics backend.
form.label.project.physics.debug_alpha = Debug Alpha
form.help.project.physics.debug_alpha = Opacity of the physics debug visualization. `0` is transparent and `1` is opaque.
form.label.project.physics.debug_scale = Debug Scale
form.help.project.physics.debug_scale = Display size of unit-length physics debug markers such as axes and contact normals. Increase it when these markers are hard to see.
form.label.project.physics.world_count = World Count
form.help.project.physics.world_count = Maximum number of physics worlds that may exist at once. Only collections capable of containing collision objects create worlds; proxy-loaded collections use separate worlds when applicable. Each world consumes additional memory.
form.label.project.physics.gravity_x = Gravity X
form.help.project.physics.gravity_x = Global gravity acceleration along the X axis, in game units per second squared. Positive values pull objects to the right.
form.label.project.physics.gravity_y = Gravity Y
form.help.project.physics.gravity_y = Global gravity acceleration along the Y axis, in game units per second squared. Negative values pull objects downward.
form.label.project.physics.gravity_z = Gravity Z
form.help.project.physics.gravity_z = Global gravity acceleration along the Z axis, in game units per second squared. Used by **3D** physics; **2D** simulation uses only X and Y.
form.label.project.physics.scale = Scale
form.help.project.physics.scale = Conversion factor from game-world units to physics meters. For example, `0.02` makes `50` game units equal one meter. Choose a value that keeps moving bodies roughly `0.1`–`10` meters in size. Range: `0.01`–`1.0`.
form.label.project.physics.allow_dynamic_transforms = Allow Dynamic Transforms
form.help.project.physics.allow_dynamic_transforms = Allows game-object position, rotation, and scale changes to be applied directly to attached **Dynamic** collision objects. Disable it if dynamic bodies should be moved only by the physics simulation.
form.label.project.physics.max_collisions = Max Collisions
form.help.project.physics.max_collisions = Maximum collision pairs reported to scripts per physics update. Additional `collision_response` messages are dropped and a warning is logged.
form.label.project.physics.max_contacts = Max Contacts
form.help.project.physics.max_contacts = Maximum contact points reported to scripts per physics update. Additional `contact_point_response` messages are dropped and a warning is logged.
form.label.project.physics.contact_impulse_limit = Contact Impulse Limit
form.help.project.physics.contact_impulse_limit = Suppresses collision and contact messages when the collision impulse is below this value. Increase it to ignore weak contacts while leaving the physical collision itself unchanged. `0` disables filtering.
form.label.project.physics.ray_cast_limit_2d = Ray Cast Limit 2D
form.help.project.physics.ray_cast_limit_2d = Maximum queued asynchronous ray-cast requests per physics world and frame when using **2D** physics. Requests beyond the limit are ignored.
form.label.project.physics.ray_cast_limit_3d = Ray Cast Limit 3D
form.help.project.physics.ray_cast_limit_3d = Maximum queued asynchronous ray-cast requests per physics world and frame when using **3D** physics. Requests beyond the limit are ignored.
form.label.project.physics.trigger_overlap_capacity = Trigger Overlap Capacity
form.help.project.physics.trigger_overlap_capacity = Maximum simultaneous trigger overlaps tracked per physics object for enter and exit messages. Excess overlaps are not tracked and produce a warning.
form.label.project.physics.velocity_threshold = Velocity Threshold
form.help.project.physics.velocity_threshold = Relative collision speed below which **2D** bodies do not bounce and are treated as inelastic. Increase it to reduce small, jittery bounces.
form.label.project.physics.max_fixed_timesteps = Max Fixed Timesteps
form.help.project.physics.max_fixed_timesteps = Maximum Bullet 3D simulation substeps during one update. It limits catch-up work after a slow frame and also affects Bullet when **Use Fixed Timestep** is disabled.

form.label.project.profiler = Profiler
form.help.project.profiler = Settings related to the runtime profiler
form.label.project.profiler.track_cpu = Track CPU
form.help.project.profiler.track_cpu = Enables CPU usage sampling on supported native platforms in **release builds** that include profiler support. Debug builds already sample where supported. Sampling adds runtime overhead; HTML5 does not support it.
form.label.project.profiler.track_detailed_memory = Detailed Memory
form.help.project.profiler.track_detailed_memory = Enables detailed memory tracking where supported; currently it matters primarily for HTML5 profiler reporting and can add significant overhead. `profiler.get_memory_usage()` remains detailed regardless.
form.label.project.profiler.enabled = Enabled
form.help.project.profiler.enabled = Starts collection for the in-game/basic profiler backend when the app launches. Disable it to avoid that collection until `profiler.enable(true)` is called. It does not disable every profiler listener or show the on-screen UI.
form.label.project.profiler.sleep_between_server_updates = Server Sleep (ms)
form.help.project.profiler.sleep_between_server_updates = Delay in milliseconds between Remotery profiler server updates. Higher values reduce update frequency and profiler overhead but make connected profiler data refresh less often.
form.label.project.profiler.performance_timeline_enabled = Performance Timeline
form.help.project.profiler.performance_timeline_enabled = Publishes Defold profiler scopes and counters to the browser Performance timeline in HTML5 builds. It requires profiler support in the build and adds profiling overhead while enabled.
form.label.project.profiler.max_sample_count = Max Sample Count
form.help.project.profiler.max_sample_count = Maximum samples recorded per thread per frame by the in-game/basic profiler backend. Excess samples are dropped. Increase this only for legitimate large profiles; unmatched native-extension scope calls can also exhaust it. Minimum: `128`.

form.label.project.render = Render
form.help.project.render = Render related settings
form.label.project.render.clear_color_red = Clear Color Red
form.help.project.render.clear_color_red = The **red** component of the clear color used when the window is created. Defold's built-in render script also uses it when clearing the frame; a custom render script need not. `0.0` contributes no red; `1.0` contributes full red intensity.
form.label.project.render.clear_color_green = Clear Color Green
form.help.project.render.clear_color_green = The **green** component of the clear color used when the window is created. Defold's built-in render script also uses it when clearing the frame; a custom render script need not. `0.0` contributes no green; `1.0` contributes full green intensity.
form.label.project.render.clear_color_blue = Clear Color Blue
form.help.project.render.clear_color_blue = The **blue** component of the clear color used when the window is created. Defold's built-in render script also uses it when clearing the frame; a custom render script need not. `0.0` contributes no blue; `1.0` contributes full blue intensity.
form.label.project.render.clear_color_alpha = Clear Color Alpha
form.help.project.render.clear_color_alpha = The **alpha** component of the clear color used when the window is created. Defold's built-in render script also uses it when clearing the frame; a custom render script need not. `0.0` is fully transparent; `1.0` is fully opaque where framebuffer alpha is used.

form.label.project.resource = Resource
form.help.project.resource = Resource loading and management related settings
form.label.project.resource.http_cache = HTTP Cache
form.help.project.resource.http_cache = **Deprecated and ignored.** HTTP caching for network-loaded resources is now controlled by **Network → HTTP Cache Enabled**. Changing this setting no longer affects the engine.
form.label.project.resource.uri = URI
form.help.project.resource.uri = Base URI from which the running engine loads compiled project resources. Leave it unset to use the project build location or bundled archive; an explicitly empty value can override fallback behavior. Use a network URI only when serving build data remotely.
form.label.project.resource.max_resources = Max Resources
form.help.project.resource.max_resources = Maximum number of distinct resources the engine can keep loaded at once. Further resource loads fail with **Out of Resources** when the limit is reached. Increasing it allows more resources at the cost of additional memory.

form.label.project.shader = Shader
form.help.project.shader = Shader related settings
form.label.project.shader.output_spirv = Output SPIR-V
form.help.project.shader.output_spirv = **Deprecated.** Forces SPIR-V shader bytecode into the build output, an option previously used for Metal and Vulkan. Modern builds include the shader formats required by the target automatically, so leave this disabled.
form.label.project.shader.exclude_gles_sm100 = Exclude GLES 2.0
form.help.project.shader.exclude_gles_sm100 = Omits the GLSL ES 1.00 shader variant used by OpenGL ES 2.0 and WebGL 1.0. Enable this only if those fallback graphics APIs are unsupported; older devices and browsers may then be unable to run the game.
form.label.project.shader.glsl_es_default_precision_float = GLSL ES float precision
form.help.project.shader.glsl_es_default_precision_float = Sets the generated default precision for unqualified floating-point values in cross-compiled GLSL ES shaders: `mediump` or `highp`. Explicit shader qualifiers take precedence; on OpenGL ES 2.0 and WebGL 1.0 fragment shaders, unsupported `highp` falls back to `mediump`.
form.label.project.shader.glsl_es_default_precision_int = GLSL ES int precision
form.help.project.shader.glsl_es_default_precision_int = Sets the generated default precision for unqualified integer values in cross-compiled GLSL ES shaders: `mediump` or `highp`. Explicit qualifiers take precedence; in OpenGL ES 2.0 and WebGL 1.0 fragment shaders, unsupported `highp` falls back to `mediump`.

form.label.project.library = Library
form.help.project.library = Settings for when this project is used as a library by another project
form.label.project.library.include_dirs = Include Dirs
form.help.project.library.include_dirs = Top-level project directories exposed to projects that depend on this library. Enter their names separated by spaces, for example `assets scripts`; assets outside these directories are not included.
form.label.project.library.defold_min_version = Defold Min Version
form.help.project.library.defold_min_version = Minimum Defold version required by projects that use this library, in `major.minor.patch` form, for example `1.11.2`. Leave empty for no requirement. Projects using an older Defold version report the library as incompatible.

form.label.project.liveupdate = Live Update
form.help.project.liveupdate = Live Update settings
form.label.project.liveupdate.enabled = Enabled
form.help.project.liveupdate.enabled = Initializes the runtime Live Update system for mounting downloaded resource archives. An App Manifest can exclude the `liveupdate` Lua module regardless of this setting.
form.label.project.liveupdate.exclude_entries_from_main_manifest = Exclude Entries from Main Manifest
form.help.project.liveupdate.exclude_entries_from_main_manifest = **Deprecated and ignored.** When publishing Live Update content, Defold always removes excluded entries from the bundled `game.dmanifest`, while `liveupdate.game.dmanifest` retains the complete resource list. Any existing value has no effect.
form.label.project.liveupdate.settings = Settings
form.help.project.liveupdate.settings = Live Update settings resource used when publishing excluded content during bundling. It selects Zip, folder, or Amazon S3 output and configures its destination. The selected file must exist when publishing.

form.label.project.native_extension = Native Extension
form.help.project.native_extension = Settings for native extensions
form.label.project.native_extension.app_manifest = App Manifest
form.help.project.native_extension.app_manifest = Select an `.appmanifest` resource to customize how the engine and native extensions are built. Its settings are merged with extension manifests and Defold's built-in engine settings. Leaving it unset still combines extension manifests with those built-in settings and does not necessarily produce a stock engine.

form.label.animationset = Animation Set
form.label.animationset.animations = Animations
form.help.animationset.animations = Animation resources combined for use by Model components. Add `.gltf` or `.glb` files or include other `.animationset` files recursively. When a glTF contains several animations, only the longest is used. IDs use source file names; repeated resources or duplicate IDs cause a build error.

form.label.camera = Camera
form.label.camera.aspect-ratio = Aspect Ratio
form.help.camera.aspect-ratio = **Perspective only.** Sets the width-to-height ratio of the view frustum. For example `1.0` is square and `1.7778` is 16:9. Ignored when **Auto Aspect Ratio** is enabled.
form.label.camera.fov = FOV
form.help.camera.fov = **Perspective only.** Sets the vertical field of view in radians. Larger values show more of the scene with stronger perspective distortion. Smaller values show less and appear zoomed in.
form.label.camera.near-z = Near Z
form.help.camera.near-z = Signed view-space depth of the near clipping plane. Geometry outside the interval between **Near Z** and **Far Z** is clipped.
form.label.camera.far-z = Far Z
form.help.camera.far-z = Signed view-space depth of the far clipping plane. A smaller interval between **Near Z** and **Far Z** improves depth-buffer precision but may clip geometry.
form.label.camera.auto-aspect-ratio = Auto Aspect Ratio
form.help.camera.auto-aspect-ratio = **Perspective only.** Uses the current window width and height to calculate the aspect ratio. This prevents the perspective view from stretching when the window shape changes and overrides **Aspect Ratio**.
form.label.camera.orthographic-projection = Orthographic Projection
form.help.camera.orthographic-projection = Switches from perspective to orthographic projection. Objects do not shrink with distance in an orthographic view, which is typically useful for 2D. **FOV** and **Aspect Ratio** no longer affect the view; **Near Z** and **Far Z** still clip by depth.
form.label.camera.orthographic-mode = Orthographic Zoom Mode
form.help.camera.orthographic-mode = **Orthographic only.** Controls how **Orthographic Zoom** adapts to the window relative to `display.width` and `display.height`. **Fixed** uses the zoom directly. **Auto Fit** shows the full design area and may reveal extra space. **Auto Cover** fills the window and may crop content.
form.label.camera.orthographic-zoom = Orthographic Zoom
form.help.camera.orthographic-zoom = **Orthographic only.** Positive zoom multiplier. Values above `1.0` zoom in and values below `1.0` zoom out. In **Fixed** mode this is the effective zoom; in **Auto Fit** and **Auto Cover** it multiplies the calculated zoom.

form.label.collectionproxy = Collection Proxy
form.label.collectionproxy.collection = Collection
form.help.collectionproxy.collection = The collection this proxy loads into a **separate game world**, with its own object namespace and physics world. After loading, `enable` initializes the world first when needed. When unloading, `unload` finalizes it first when needed; explicit `init`, `disable`, and `final` messages remain available for manual lifecycle control.
form.label.collectionproxy.exclude = Exclude
form.help.collectionproxy.exclude = Excludes this proxy's content from the main bundle when publishing Live Update content, including resources that are not unique to one excluded proxy. Publish and deliver the content, then make it available before loading the proxy. **Build and Run** from the editor does not exclude it.

form.label.render = Render
form.label.render.script = Script
form.help.render.script = The Lua render script that controls what is drawn, in which order, and with which view, projection, render targets, materials, and GPU state. Its `init()` runs once, `update()` runs every frame after messages to `@render` are dispatched, and `on_message()` handles those messages.
form.label.render.render-resources = Resources
form.help.render.render-resources = Named materials, render targets, and compute programs to load and expose to the render script. Use each name in render API calls such as `render.enable_material()`, `render.set_render_target()`, or `render.set_compute()`; a resource must be listed here before the script can use it.
form.label.render.render-resources.name = Name
form.label.render.render-resources.resource = Resource

form.label.render-target = Render Target
form.label.render-target.color-attachments = Color Attachments
form.help.render-target.color-attachments = Defines the color textures that receive rendered output. Each row creates one attachment with its own size and pixel format. Use matching dimensions for all attachments for portability across graphics backends. Up to `4` are supported.
form.label.render-target.color-attachments.width = Width
form.label.render-target.color-attachments.height = Height
form.label.render-target.color-attachments.format = Format
form.label.render-target.depth-stencil-attachment-width = Depth/Stencil Width
form.help.render-target.depth-stencil-attachment-width = Width in pixels of the shared depth/stencil attachment. Set both width and height above `0` to create the attachment; leaving both at `0` disables it.
form.label.render-target.depth-stencil-attachment-height = Depth/Stencil Height
form.help.render-target.depth-stencil-attachment-height = Height in pixels of the shared depth/stencil attachment. Set both width and height above `0` to create the attachment; leaving both at `0` disables it.
form.label.render-target.depth-stencil-attachment-texture-storage = Depth Texture Storage
form.help.render-target.depth-stencil-attachment-texture-storage = Stores depth data in a texture instead of a render buffer so the depth attachment can be bound and sampled by a shader. It is addressed as `graphics.BUFFER_TYPE_DEPTH_BIT`. Stencil always uses non-sampleable render-buffer storage.
form.label.performance.cache_capacity = Cache Capacity
form.help.performance.cache_capacity = Maximum number of evictable calculation results the editor caches. Retained results do not count toward this capacity, so it is not a total cache-size limit. Larger values can avoid recalculation but use more memory. Use `0` to disable or `-1` for unlimited; restart after changing it.
form.label.performance.non_editable_directories = Non-Editable Directories
form.help.performance.non_editable_directories = Project directories whose contents are read-only in the editor but remain available to references and builds. Use this for externally generated content to reduce project load time and memory use. Enter project-relative paths that start with `/` and do not end with `/`, for example `/generated`; each path includes all its subdirectories. Restart the editor after changing this setting.
form.label.extensions.build_server = Build Server
form.help.extensions.build_server = Base URL for custom engine builds. The prefilled Defold server depends on the Editor release channel, and the personal Extensions preference overrides this shared value. Extension source and resources are uploaded only when no matching custom engine is cached, so use a trusted endpoint.

form.label.display-profiles = Display Profiles
form.label.display-profiles.auto-layout-selection = Auto Layout Selection
form.help.display-profiles.auto-layout-selection = Controls whether Defold automatically chooses among layouts present in each GUI scene. Selection runs when the scene is created and when display size changes. Disable it to use `gui.set_layout()` instead.
form.label.display-profiles.profile = Profile
form.help.display-profiles.profile = Names a GUI layout and supplies qualifier sets for it. A qualifier may list several device-model prefixes; any matching prefix is eligible. Candidates are scored by orientation, area, and aspect ratio, with opposite-orientation candidates used as fallback. Only layouts present in the GUI scene participate; **Default** is used if none match.
form.label.display-profiles.profile.qualifiers = Qualifiers
form.label.display-profiles.profile.qualifiers.width = Width
form.label.display-profiles.profile.qualifiers.height = Height
form.label.display-profiles.profile.qualifiers.device-models = Device Models

form.label.input-binding = Input Bindings
form.label.input-binding.key-trigger = Key Triggers
form.help.input-binding.key-trigger = Maps a single physical keyboard key to a named action delivered to input-focused scripts and GUI scripts through `on_input()`. Key actions report `pressed`, `released`, and `repeated`; use Text Triggers instead when you need typed characters.
form.label.input-binding.key-trigger.input = Input
form.label.input-binding.key-trigger.action = Action
form.label.input-binding.mouse-trigger = Mouse Triggers
form.help.input-binding.mouse-trigger = Maps a mouse button or wheel direction to a named action delivered through `on_input()`. Button actions report `pressed`, `released`, and `repeated`; wheel actions report `value`. Mouse movement is unbound (`action_id` is `nil`) but is emitted only when at least one mouse trigger exists.
form.label.input-binding.mouse-trigger.input = Input
form.label.input-binding.mouse-trigger.action = Action
form.label.input-binding.gamepad-trigger = Gamepad Triggers
form.help.input-binding.gamepad-trigger = Maps a standard gamepad button, stick direction, trigger, connection event, or raw input to a named action delivered through `on_input()`. Hardware is normalized by the project Gamepads mapping; unidentified controllers provide only Connected, Disconnected, and Raw. `action.gamepad` identifies the source controller.
form.label.input-binding.gamepad-trigger.input = Input
form.label.input-binding.gamepad-trigger.action = Action
form.label.input-binding.touch-trigger = Touch Triggers
form.help.input-binding.touch-trigger = Maps `TOUCH_MULTI` to a named action delivered through `on_input()` with all current touch points in `action.touch`. Available on iOS, Android, and mobile HTML5. Single touch is not configured here: binding `MOUSE_BUTTON_LEFT` or `MOUSE_BUTTON_1` creates it automatically, and multi-touch must use a different action name.
form.label.input-binding.touch-trigger.input = Input
form.label.input-binding.touch-trigger.action = Action
form.label.input-binding.text-trigger = Text Triggers
form.help.input-binding.text-trigger = Maps committed or IME-composition text to a named action delivered through `on_input()`. Both **Text** and **Marked Text** put their text in `action.text`; these actions omit ordinary fields such as `pressed`, `released`, `repeated`, and `value`. Use Key Triggers for physical keys.
form.label.input-binding.text-trigger.input = Input
form.label.input-binding.text-trigger.action = Action

form.label.gamepads = Gamepads
form.label.gamepads.driver = Gamepad
form.help.gamepads.driver = Maps one gamepad model to Defold inputs. **Platform** filters mappings at build time; **Device** identifies the controller at runtime. **Dead zone** filters small stick movement and **Map** assigns raw controls. Unmatched controllers expose only the **Connected**, **Disconnected**, and **Raw** fallback actions.
form.label.gamepads.driver.device = Device
form.label.gamepads.driver.platform = Platform
form.label.gamepads.driver.dead-zone = Dead zone
form.label.gamepads.driver.map = Map
form.label.gamepads.driver.map.input = Input
form.label.gamepads.driver.map.type = Type
form.label.gamepads.driver.map.index = Index
form.label.gamepads.driver.map.negate = Negate
form.label.gamepads.driver.map.scale = Scale
form.label.gamepads.driver.map.clamp = Clamp
form.label.gamepads.driver.map.hat-mask = Hat Mask

form.label.texture-profiles = Texture Profiles
form.label.texture-profiles.path-settings = Path Settings
form.help.texture-profiles.path-settings = Maps Ant-style path patterns to named profiles. Entries are checked from top to bottom and the first matching entry selects its profile. Put specific patterns before general patterns. If no pattern matches then Defold applies no profile.
form.label.texture-profiles.path-settings.path = Path
form.label.texture-profiles.path-settings.profile = Profile
form.label.texture-profiles.profiles = Profiles
form.help.texture-profiles.profiles = Defines named processing profiles selected by Path Settings. Each platform entry contains alternative output formats plus settings for compression, mipmaps, maximum size, and alpha premultiplication. `OS_ID_GENERIC` applies on every platform. The engine selects a supported format at runtime; max size `0` disables only the profile's size limit.
form.label.texture-profiles.profiles.platforms = Platforms
form.label.texture-profiles.profiles.platforms.formats = Formats
form.label.texture-profiles.profiles.platforms.formats.format = Format
form.label.texture-profiles.profiles.platforms.formats.compressor = Compressor
form.label.texture-profiles.profiles.platforms.formats.compressor-preset = Compressor Preset
form.label.texture-profiles.profiles.platforms.mipmaps = Mipmaps
form.label.texture-profiles.profiles.platforms.max-texture-size = Max Texture Size
form.label.texture-profiles.profiles.platforms.premultiply-alpha = Premultiply Alpha

form.label.factory = Factory
form.label.factory.prototype = Prototype
form.help.factory.prototype = The game object prototype this component spawns when `factory.create()` is called. Position, rotation, script properties, and scale can be overridden for each new instance.
form.label.factory.load-dynamically = Load Dynamically
form.help.factory.load-dynamically = Defers loading the prototype resources until `factory.create()` or `factory.load()` is called. This can reduce initial loading and memory use, but creating before an asynchronous load completes may cause a hitch. After `factory.load()`, call `factory.unload()` when those references are no longer needed.
form.label.factory.dynamic-prototype = Dynamic Prototype
form.help.factory.dynamic-prototype = Allows `factory.set_prototype()` to change which game object the factory spawns at runtime. If the previous prototype was loaded with `factory.load()`, call `factory.unload()` before switching. Dynamic prototypes disable component-count optimization and may use more memory.

form.label.collectionfactory = Collection Factory
form.label.collectionfactory.prototype = Prototype
form.help.collectionfactory.prototype = The collection whose game objects and parent-child hierarchy this component spawns into the current game world with `collectionfactory.create()`.
form.label.collectionfactory.load-dynamically = Load Dynamically
form.help.collectionfactory.load-dynamically = Defers loading the prototype's resources until they are needed; the resources are still included in the application bundle. Calling `collectionfactory.create()` before `collectionfactory.load()` loads them synchronously and may cause a hitch. Use `collectionfactory.load()` to load asynchronously and `collectionfactory.unload()` to release the factory's references when no longer needed.
form.label.collectionfactory.dynamic-prototype = Dynamic Prototype
form.help.collectionfactory.dynamic-prototype = Allows `collectionfactory.set_prototype()` to change the collection spawned at runtime. If the previous prototype was loaded with `collectionfactory.load()`, call `collectionfactory.unload()` before switching. Dynamic prototypes disable component-count optimization and may reserve more memory.

form.label.sound = Sound
form.label.sound.sound = Sound
form.help.sound.sound = Audio resource played by this component. Supported resources use WAV, Ogg Vorbis or Ogg Opus audio; Ogg Opus requires its optional decoder in the application manifest.
form.label.sound.looping = Loop
form.help.sound.looping = Repeats the sound according to **Loop Count**. When disabled the sound plays once.
form.label.sound.loopcount = Loop Count
form.help.sound.loopcount = Number of repeats after the initial playback. `0` loops until explicitly stopped; valid values are `0` through `127`. Only used when **Loop** is enabled.
form.label.sound.group = Group
form.help.sound.group = Routes the sound to a named mixer group so its level can be controlled with the sound API.
form.label.sound.gain = Gain
form.help.sound.gain = Non-negative component gain. `0.0` is silent and `1.0` is unity gain. With linear gain, values above `1.0` amplify and the combined playback, group, and master gains may clip.
form.label.sound.pan = Pan
form.help.sound.pan = Stereo position from `-1.0` at the left through `0.0` at the center to `1.0` at the right.
form.label.sound.speed = Speed
form.help.sound.speed = Component playback-rate multiplier clamped to `0.0`–`50.0`. `1.0` is normal speed. It is multiplied by the speed supplied when playback starts, and the resulting rate is also clamped to the supported range.

form.label.light = Light
form.label.light.type = Type
form.label.light.color = Color
form.label.light.intensity = Intensity
form.label.light.range = Range
form.label.light.inner-cone-angle = Inner Cone Angle
form.label.light.outer-cone-angle = Outer Cone Angle

form.label.liveupdate.liveupdate = Live Update
form.label.liveupdate.liveupdate.mode = Mode
form.help.liveupdate.liveupdate.mode = Selects the publisher used for excluded resources when **Publish Live Update Content** is enabled during bundling. **Zip** creates an archive, **Folder** stages individual compiled files, and **Amazon** uploads them to S3.
form.label.liveupdate.amazon = Amazon
form.label.liveupdate.liveupdate.amazon-credential-profile = Credential Profile
form.help.liveupdate.liveupdate.amazon-credential-profile = AWS credentials profile used for uploads. The Editor reads the first existing file named by `AWS_SHARED_CREDENTIALS_FILE`, then `AWS_CREDENTIAL_PROFILES_FILE`, falling back to `~/.aws/credentials`; unset or nonexistent paths are skipped.
form.label.liveupdate.liveupdate.amazon-bucket = Bucket
form.help.liveupdate.liveupdate.amazon-bucket = Name of the Amazon S3 bucket that receives excluded Live Update resources when publishing. The selected profile must be able to inspect and write to it; configure read access separately so game clients can download the published content.
form.label.liveupdate.liveupdate.amazon-prefix = Prefix
form.help.liveupdate.liveupdate.amazon-prefix = Required S3 object-key prefix placed before each resource hash, for example `my-game/liveupdate`. Use distinct prefixes to separate projects or releases within one bucket.
form.label.liveupdate.zip = Zip
form.label.liveupdate.liveupdate.save-zip-in-bundle-folder = Save in Bundle Folder
form.help.liveupdate.liveupdate.save-zip-in-bundle-folder = Moves the generated Live Update Zip archive into the application bundle output after bundling. When enabled, this final destination takes precedence over **Output Directory**.
form.label.liveupdate.liveupdate.zip-filepath = Output Directory
form.help.liveupdate.liveupdate.zip-filepath = Directory where the generated Live Update Zip archive is written. Relative paths resolve from the project root. Leave empty to use the project root. **Save in Bundle Folder** takes precedence as the final destination.
form.label.liveupdate.liveupdate.zip-filename = Filename
form.help.liveupdate.liveupdate.zip-filename = Name of the generated Live Update Zip archive. The `.zip` extension is appended if omitted. Leave empty to use an automatically generated name.
form.title.liveupdate.liveupdate.zip-filepath = Select Zip Output Directory
form.label.liveupdate.liveupdate.zip-compression-level = Compression Level
form.help.liveupdate.liveupdate.zip-compression-level = Zip compression level from `0` to `9`. Higher values reduce archive size but take longer to create; `0` disables compression.
form.label.liveupdate.folder = Folder
form.label.liveupdate.liveupdate.save-folder-in-bundle-folder = Save in Bundle Folder
form.help.liveupdate.liveupdate.save-folder-in-bundle-folder = After publishing to the staging **Output Directory**, moves the generated resource folder beside the application bundle and replaces a destination folder with the same name.
form.label.liveupdate.liveupdate.output-directory = Output Directory
form.help.liveupdate.liveupdate.output-directory = Staging parent directory where Folder mode first creates its resource folder, even when **Save in Bundle Folder** later moves it beside the bundle. Relative paths resolve from the project root; when empty, the project root is used.
form.title.liveupdate.liveupdate.output-directory = Select Output Directory
form.label.liveupdate.liveupdate.output-folder-name = Output Folder
form.help.liveupdate.liveupdate.output-folder-name = Name of the folder containing the Live Update manifest and resource files. When empty, Defold uses `defold_resources_<platform><Unix timestamp>`. Reusing an existing staging folder does not remove stale files from earlier publishes.
form.label.liveupdate.manifest = Manifest
form.label.liveupdate.liveupdate.publickey = Public Key
form.help.liveupdate.liveupdate.publickey = Deprecated. Manifest public keys are no longer used and this setting causes a fatal project error. It formerly selected the X.509 DER-encoded RSA public key paired with the private signing key to verify a Live Update manifest.
form.title.liveupdate.liveupdate.publickey = Select Manifest Public Key
form.label.liveupdate.liveupdate.privatekey = Private Key
form.help.liveupdate.liveupdate.privatekey = Deprecated. Manifest private keys are no longer used and this setting causes a fatal project error. It formerly selected the PKCS #8 DER-encoded RSA private key paired with the public verification key to sign a Live Update manifest. Private keys must be kept secret.
form.title.liveupdate.liveupdate.privatekey = Select Manifest Private Key
form.label.liveupdate.liveupdate.supported-versions = Supported Engine Versions
form.help.liveupdate.liveupdate.supported-versions = Additional engine version strings that may mount this Live Update manifest. Enter them as a comma-separated list. The build engine version is always included. Mounting fails with `ENGINE_VERSION_MISMATCH` when the running engine matches none of them.

form.label.material = Material
form.label.material.name = Name
form.help.material.name = Internal name embedded in this Material resource. A Render resource assigns its own identifier when it includes the material; that separate identifier is used by APIs such as `render.enable_material()`.
form.label.material.vertex-program = Vertex Program
form.help.material.vertex-program = The `.vp` shader that runs once for each vertex. It must produce the final clip-space position and may pass varying values to the fragment program.
form.label.material.fragment-program = Fragment Program
form.help.material.fragment-program = The `.fp` shader that runs for each rasterized fragment. It typically samples textures and combines varying values and constants to produce the output color.
form.label.material.attributes = Vertex Attributes
form.help.material.attributes = Vertex inputs expected by the vertex program. **Semantic Type** identifies engine or component data, **Coordinate Space** controls supported semantic transformations, and **Value** supplies constant data when no matching component stream overrides it. **Step Function** selects per-vertex or per-instance delivery.
form.label.material.attributes.semantic-type = Semantic Type
form.label.material.attributes.step-function = Step Function
form.label.material.attributes.coordinate-space = Coordinate Space
form.label.material.attributes.data-type = Data Type
form.label.material.attributes.vector-type = Vector Type
form.label.material.attributes.value = Value
form.label.material.attributes.normalize = Normalize
form.label.material.vertex-constants = Vertex Constants
form.help.material.vertex-constants = Uniform values passed to the vertex program. Each `Name` must exactly match a uniform used by the shader. Built-in types supply transforms or time while user types provide an initial value that component APIs or a render constant buffer can override. Per-component values may split batches.
form.label.material.vertex-constants.name = Name
form.label.material.vertex-constants.type = Type
form.label.material.vertex-constants.value = Value
form.label.material.fragment-constants = Fragment Constants
form.help.material.fragment-constants = Uniform values passed to the fragment program. Each `Name` must exactly match a uniform used by the shader. Built-in types supply engine data while user types provide an initial value that component APIs or a render constant buffer can override. Per-component values may split batches.
form.label.material.fragment-constants.name = Name
form.label.material.fragment-constants.type = Type
form.label.material.fragment-constants.value = Value
form.label.material.samplers = Samplers
form.help.material.samplers = Texture sampling settings used by the shader. Each `Name` must exactly match a sampler uniform. Wrap modes handle coordinates outside the texture while filters and anisotropy control texel selection. Textures come from component slots or render-script bindings. Unconfigured samplers use the project filtering defaults where supported.
form.label.material.samplers.name = Name
form.label.material.samplers.wrap-u = Wrap U
form.label.material.samplers.wrap-v = Wrap V
form.label.material.samplers.filter-min = Min Filter
form.label.material.samplers.filter-mag = Mag Filter
form.label.material.samplers.max-anisotropy = Max Anisotropy
form.label.material.tags = Tags
form.help.material.tags = Identifiers used by render predicates to select components drawn with this material. A predicate containing several tags matches only objects that have all of them. Each material can have at most `32` tags.
form.label.material.vertex-space = Vertex Space
form.help.material.vertex-space = Controls whether vertices reach the vertex program in **World** or **Local** object space. **World** is mandatory for Sprite, Tile Map, ParticleFX, Label, and GUI components. **Local** requires the shader to apply the world transform and supports GPU-skinned or instanced models.
form.label.material.max-page-count = Max Atlas Pages
form.help.material.max-page-count = Maximum paged-atlas pages supported by this material's fallback samplers on graphics APIs without texture arrays. It must cover every assigned paged atlas. This is not a general texture-array layer limit and does not page an atlas by itself; use `0` for ordinary textures.

form.label.compute = Compute
form.label.compute.compute-program = Program
form.help.compute.compute-program = The `.cp` program that performs this resource's GPU work. Add the `.compute` resource to a Render resource, then select and dispatch it from the render script. At runtime, check `graphics.CONTEXT_FEATURE_COMPUTE_SHADER`; backend names alone do not guarantee support.
form.label.compute.constants = Constants
form.help.compute.constants = Initial uniform values for the compute program. `compute.set_constants()` changes the resource's persistent constants, while a constant buffer supplied to a dispatch overrides values for that dispatch only. **Name** must exactly match a uniform in the `.cp` program.
form.label.compute.constants.name = Name
form.label.compute.constants.type = Type
form.label.compute.constants.value = Value
form.label.compute.samplers = Samplers
form.help.compute.samplers = Sampling settings for sampler uniforms declared in the `.cp` program. They do not apply to storage images. **Name** must exactly match the sampler uniform; bind its texture separately from the render script before dispatch.
form.label.compute.samplers.name = Name
form.label.compute.samplers.wrap-u = Wrap U
form.label.compute.samplers.wrap-v = Wrap V
form.label.compute.samplers.filter-min = Min Filter
form.label.compute.samplers.filter-mag = Mag Filter
form.label.compute.samplers.max-anisotropy = Max Anisotropy

